{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1075297-ash-dies-at-the-end-an-actual-play","id":1075297,"title":"Ash Dies at the End - an Actual Play","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-08T16:43:53-07:00","id":1075297,"title":"Ash Dies at the End - an Actual Play","content":"Back in 2013, Axelgear, myself, and two other players began a game of Mage: the Awakening. Our first. Initially, there was nothing that stood out about it. Most of us were floundering because we hadn\u2019t really grasped the nature of the setting, or the themes inherent within, and we all made the rookie mistake of not coordinating on what our characters wanted or where the game was going. Stories were a bit disconnected, characters didn\u2019t play well off each other, and at one point an entire plotline was scrapped and resolved off-camera.<br /> <br /> But something happened. Near the middle-to-end point, we began to get a better appreciation for the setting, and for what our characters stood for. Things became more complex. Characters became more nuanced. We began to comprehend just what the setting was going for. Unfortunately, due to both time schedules and a complete disconnect by players in terms of theme, the unified game died in a bunch of fire (not entirely a metaphor). From that, three different solo games began, two of which continue into today.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sharing this now, years out, because I feel they can present some insight into approaching the setting, dos and don\u2019ts. I also do it because these games ended up being some of the most interesting and most crazy experiences I\u2019ve had. Sometimes they were unbearably human, and sometimes entertainingly over-the-top. I'm also doing this because Axelgear won't stop encouraging me to.<br /> <br /> This AP will be separated into three chronicles, each detailing a specific era in both the games and their styles, and all of them following from the perspective of an Obrimos by the shadow name of Ash. Part of this will be transcribed from memory\u2014mostly the earliest examples\u2014and part will be done from logs.<br /> <br /> With that said, on to the characters of note:<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T16:44:23-07:00","id":1075298,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">CHRONICLE I: THE THREE-HEADED DRAGON</span></b><br /> The first game, and the most tumultuous. We didn\u2019t \u2018get\u2019 Mage too well at first. Ash essentially wanted to advocate as if science-magic was still a thing that existed from Ascension, Kismet\u2019s player wasn\u2019t into much of it, and Midas\u2019s player was more into exploring old ruins than dealing with human costs and hubris. Most of this is reconstructed from memory, and a lot of it will be retconned over the course of the telling so that it\u2019ll make sense. I\u2019ll note what we did wrong and when I\u2019ve taken liberties for sake of cohesion.<br /> <br /> Our first chronicle begins in Oregon with the Cabal of the Three-Headed Dragon, a name they wouldn\u2019t adopt for some time. Three recently-Awakened, each with atypical skill in magic, and in whom several significant mages see promise\u2014more than just potential, more an omen\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>The Players</b><br /> Argentum Everto/\u00c6/Ash<br /> An Obrimos in his mid-twenties, Ash has a master\u2019s in theoretical physics, is incredibly intelligent, and has an uncanny skill with firearms. Unfortunately, social he is not. His Awakening took the form of a mystery play in which he ignored any number of fantastical creatures to finish some divine mathematical formula and then burn his house down. At the start of the game, he\u2019s optimistic to step into a world more meaningful than the one he grew up in. Despite having sensibilities more suited to the Free Council, he joins the Silver Ladder for their ideals.<br /> <br /> Midas<br /> David was a chemistry teacher. A Moros, he Awoke in a car crash, and after some Paradox-related gaffes met his mentor, Adelaide. Prior to the start of the game he\u2019d had his own set of adventures, in which he found a fondness for alchemy and earned the patronage of a Supernal being by the name of Gur Aryeh. In many ways he embodies the \u2018gentleman explorer\u2019 aesthetic. He originally hails from Chicago. He\u2019s charming and emotionally-intelligent, with a preference for swords if violence becomes necessary. He\u2019s a recent member of the Mysterium.<br /> <br /> Kismet<br /> Kismet was a police sketch artist who Awoke as an Acanthus during a frantic moment where she felt her life was spiraling out of her control. Unfortunately, suddenly stepping into a secret world of mysteries and horrors is unlikely to help that. Perhaps even more risky is her choice to join the Guardians of the Veil.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Supporting Cast</b><br /> <u><i>The Mentors</i></u><br /> Goch \u2013 A dark-skinned man who somehow knew exactly where to find Ash shortly after his Awakening. His approach to teaching Ash is hands-off\u2014though that may simply be because he has no idea how to do it.<br /> <br /> Adelaide \u2013 Midas\u2019s mentor. A woman just past middle age, she\u2019s a member of the Sodality of Tor. Not long after their introduction, she also comes to fulfill the role for Kismet, as well as be a teacher of her Legacy.<br /> <br /> The Good Father \u2013 Kismet\u2019s first mentor. Secretly a Clavicularus, he skipped town when Kismet found out what he was and they realized their arrangement wouldn\u2019t work with her convictions as a Guardian.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><i>The Consilium</i></u><br /> NOTE: The state of the Oregon Consilium is the perfect example of the setting issues we experienced as our first game. It was atypically large, lacked a hierarch, and had representatives from caucuses instead of singular cabals. None of us, ST included, realized this was odd until long after the fact. It was composed of:<br /> <br /> Orcus \u2013 In his nineties, Orcus has been a Mage and a member of the Mysterium for a very long time. At least a third-degree master, he\u2019s the unspoken power behind the Oregon Consilium. His face is almost always obscured by a hood.<br /> <br /> Marx \u2013 Young, vibrant, a member of the Free Council, and a bit of an anarchist, Marx is the rebel-in-office. She wears a pair of large gauntlets, and has extensive drug connections. As many mages do.<br /> <br /> Tartarus \u2013 A Guardian just past middle-age. He\u2019s seen some shit, and has the scars and temperament to prove it.<br /> <br /> Seshat \u2013 A businesswoman and member of the Silver Ladder. Largely the source of any resources the Consilium required.<br /> <br /> Dagda \u2013 Dagda didna do shit<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><i>Other Characters</i></u><br /> Pathos \u2013 A stage magician at a nightclub, Pathos is a member of the Silver Ladder and an Obrimos. She quickly becomes the most important person to Ash, and plays many roles in his life\u2014confidante, friend, ally, nursemaid, host. Enabler.<br /> <br /> Gavril \u2013 A fortune-teller from Siberia, divining the future and past from a strange stone found near the Stony Tunguska River.<br /> <br /> Argos \u2013 A spirit hound from a Chicago spirit court, Argos sniffs out Abyssal corruption. He serves as Midas\u2019s ally, guide, and familiar.<br /> <br /> Malthus \u2013 Malthus is a powerful Moros. In the 80s he showed immense talent and potential alongside arrogant and radical streaks. At some point this led him down darker avenues of power. The extent of his acts and depravities are only known to him, but he eventually turned Tremere, and earned a spear through his heart from Tartarus for it. Somehow, that hasn't stopped him, as he's returned, has amassed a small cult, and is building a Ladder from stolen souls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cFred\u201d \u2013 L\u0307\u0350\u0304\u033d\u036d\u033d\u0352\u033e\u0337\u0360\u0315\u0338\u0321\u032c\u0331\u0353\u0329\u0333\u0347\u0359\u0353\u032c\u0353\u0318\u032d\u0320\u0359\u0330\u0324\u031fe\u0309\u036e\u030a\u0305\u034c\u0305\u0302\u0336\u0328\u0315\u035d\u035f\u031f\u0318\u0323\u0316\u0330\u033a \u032a\u032c\u0332t\u030f\u034c\u033d\u0351\u036f\u0321\u0336\u0340\u0347\u032f\u032b\u032c\u0326\u032e\u0348\u0319\u0353\u031f\u0333\u0353\u033b\u0332 \u0352\u0367\u0350\u0363\u0310\u036e\u0365\u030b\u0366\u0357\u0367\u036d\u0357\u0363\u0346\u033f\u0360\u035e\u0340\u033a\u032f\u031f\u033a\u0353\u0356\u0359\u0323\u0332\u032a\u0324\u0320\u0319\u034e\u0332\u0324m\u0365\u030a\u0301\u0350\u0366\u0314\u033e\u0369\u0363\u0340\u0331\u031e\u0359\u035a \u031f\u031d\u033ae\u030f\u0357\u0350\u030c\u0307\u030b\u0350\u036e\u031a\u036f\u0307\u031a\u036c\u0322\u034f\u0338\u0328\u035f\u0349\u032b\u0326\u0348\u032e\u035a\u031c\u031e\u0329\u0326\u031f \u0344\u0313\u030d\u0305\u0369\u036f\u036b\u034b\u0313\u0357\u0307\u0301\u034b\u0314\u033f\u0336\u0324\u032b\u032a\u0325\u031d\u035at\u036d\u0342\u030c\u0302\u0311\u0300\u030c\u036a\u0358\u0358\u0332\u0359\u032c\u0356\u0320\u032a\u032ee\u030d\u030b\u0364\u0346\u0368\u034b\u0344\u0313\u0366 \u036b\u0306\u0313\u0301\u0300\u036b\u0311\u035b\u030d\u0337\u0361\u035f\u0354\u0331\u035a\u