1\u0369\u0311\u0358\u034f\u0328\u0322\u0331\u0320\u0317\u0331\u032e\u032c\u0326\u032e\u0347\u0354\u0325s\u036c\u035b\u033d\u0368\u0302\u030a\u036f\u0351\u0311\u030d\u0368\u0312\u034c\u0366\u034a\u0362\u0489\u032c\u0324\u0326\u032f\u0317\u0316\u033c\u031f\u0354 \u0324\u031e\u034d\u032ae\u0308\u0365\u0306\u0367\u0312\u034a\u030a\u0305\u034a\u030c\u033e\u0350\u0369\u0365\u033f\u0304\u0309\u036f\u0343\u034f\u034f\u0334\u033b\u0325\u0355\u032d\u035a\u0325\u034d\u0324\u0317\u035a\u0324\u032d\u0317\u033a\u0348\u031f\u0325c\u036f\u0303\u0366\u0350\u036c \u030f\u0351\u030d\u0363\u0365\u0352\u036c\u0352\u0363\u030c\u0312\u0302\u0335\u0335\u0328\u032e\u0316\u0333\u0347\u0325\u0353\u0317\u0325\u033b\u0348\u0353\u032d\u0356\u032d\u0330\u031f\u0345\u0326r\u0304\u030f\u030d\u0308\u0341\u0338\u0338\u0318\u032f\u033c\u0330\u0324\u032c\u0319\u0345\u0356 \u0354\u032d\u0324\u034d\u032e\u0326e\u0312\u036a\u0344\u030c\u0357\u0360\u0327\u0315\u033c\u034e\u0323\u0324\u0319\u031e\u032ct\u0306\u0369\u0346\u030c\u035e\u0361\u0340\u031c\u034d\u031f\u035a\u0329\u034e\u035a\u032a\u0324\u031e\u0325\u0348\u0359s\u0343\u0311\u034b\u036e\u0322\u0334 \u035f\u034d\u033c\u034e\u032a\u0348\u0333\u0329\u0347\u033c\u031d\u0316\u032a\u033c\u034e\u0319\u035a\u032b\u031e\u0356","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 06-07-2017, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T16:44:57-07:00","id":1075299,"title":"","content":"Reserved for future things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T16:58:26-07:00","id":1075306,"title":"","content":"I, for one, look forward to my worst mistakes being made public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T13:24:58-07:00","id":1075572,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Chapter 1: Blood and Spiders<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Part 1</span></span><br /> <br /> It's evening, and Kismet, Ash, and Midas all find themselves invited (more like called) to a gathering in the woods, hosted by the eldest and most powerful member of the Consilium, a Mystagogue by the name of Orcus<i>. </i>They're told that the other counselors would be in attendance, and to present themselves accordingly. <i>Somehow</i> word of this found its way to Midas's mentor, Adelaide, and <i>somehow</i> a number of other Mages found their way to the spot, and are making an event of it. Someone has made a soulstone, and a number of mages--mostly the younger ones--are busy showing off and generally making idiots of themselves.</span><br /> <br /> Ash looks around at everyone, a little confused, but without judgement. Midas is no stranger to these things. Kismet is keeping to herself, otherwise uninvolved with all that's going on. The members of the council are off discussing things amongst themselves--well, all but Orcus is. Orcus is busy speaking with Adelaide, and while the hood makes discerning his expression impossible, Adelaide's age-lined face is clearly excited.<br /> <br /> Roughly an hour after all the intended guests have arrived, the council pulls Ash, Midas, and Kismet aside. As tends to happen when the heads of the Consilium uniformly draw their attention to you, suddenly the three mages are now the center of everyone's attention. The faces of the council all wear different expressions, and from the way Orcus takes the lead in talking, it's fairly clear whatever this is, it belongs to him and they're simply cooperating.<br /> <br /> Orcus speaks, and the three mages listen. He outlines what he wants from them: all three have been solo acts up until this point, and from what he knows he thinks that the three of them would work well together. Midas is already experienced, and Ash and Kismet's individual talents might benefit from that guidance. Midas catches Adelaide from the corner of his eye; she's smiling in a way that's more unsettling than warm. He writes it off.<br /> <br /> Orcus continues: there's a task he needs done, something he's been intending to take care of for some time but hasn't managed to do so owing to the fact that he's 93 and breathing is getting harder. He doesn't say as much in those words, but a coughing fit which is stopped by a magical pat on the back by the Silver Ladder councilor--Seshat--says it for him. He feels that, owing to the simplicity of it, it'd be a good way for the mages to get an idea of each other, and hopefully see how well they work together.<br /> <br /> Ash looks over at the other two. One's dressed like he stepped out a book on victorian-era fashion. The other looks far too casual to be what she is. And here he is, wearing a suit a size too small he'd borrowed from Goch, eyes sunken from a few weeks of increasingly-troubled sleep. Still, he smiles and waves at them, and they return the gesture. The three of them agree to lend Orcus a hand.<br /> <br /> Somehow, all three of them resist the urge to make a joke about accepting a quest.<br /> <br /> Marx--a councilor from the Free Council, a title and affiliation that makes addressing her difficult--steps forward, and the heavy gauntlets she wears dig into the air. A moment later she wrenches open a hole in space, on the other side of which the newly-formed cabal and see an aged mesoamerican temple with its ziggurat-like tiers. Marx looks smug at their surprised reactions, Ash and Kismet especially (their jaws have been hanging open), and shoos them through it.<br /> <br /> As the cabal passes through the portal, it hits them: the sudden change in humidity and temperature that makes Ash and Midas wish they'd dressed differently. They approach the Temple, and Midas takes point--he's had the most experience with these sorts of things, having delved into a ruin or two already which may hold any number of magical items or creatures inside. As they climb the steps and reach the top, this decision is validated. They find a hole descending into darkness, stone having crumbled away, and through it Midas senses something atypical through it, having invested some study into the Spirit Arcanum. The three look at each other, and descend into darkness.<br /> <br /> As the cabal reaches the bottom, they all sense that things have changed, and Midas confirms it: they've passed through a verge. They're in the Shadow now, something which makes Ash especially nervous. This is well outside his frames of reference, and he clutches his pistol tightly.<br /> <br /> The cabal passes through a carved cavern, the walls covered in murals and reliefs definitely not in-line with any native american iconography any of them are familiar with. Unfortunately, they're so busy gawking at the inconsistent markings that they don't notice that they've begun walking over one, and that there's an odd patterning to it. Too late, Kismet's foot steps on a trigger. The ceiling begins to rush down at them.<br /> <br /> Ash freezes for a moment, trying to make sense of this. It's like something out of Indiana Jones, and there's something severely ridiculous about it all--why would the makers of this place include this? How would they have set up this mechanism? Why would they do it here? It's both too high-tech and low-tech all at once to make sense. He's pulled out of his confused contemplations by the sound of one of the others yelling, and reflexively he raises his hand, telekinetically stopping and holding the ceiling in place with Forces.<br /> <br /> After clearing the ceiling trap, the cabal finds itself much more cautious, actually looking at where they're going. They manage to dodge another floor switch, and proceed further into the hidden temple. As they go further, the halls narrow. Cobwebs begin to cover the walls and ceiling, and eventually they find themselves entering into a larger chamber. It's lit a soft blue, and it's so thick with dust and gossamer webs that it almost look like they've stepped into a cloudscape.<br /> <br /> It's then that Midas notices something moving in the soft light, and draws all their attention to it. It emerges from the fluffy clouds of blue-white, and whatever peace this place might've had is shattered. The cabal finds itself face-to-face with a horse-sized spider, and from the way its rushing towards them it is not happy that they've intruded.<br /> <br /> Ash reacts first, with the primal terror of an arachnophobe, and draws his gun. He weaves an imago, and a gout of flame fires from its barrel, scorching and burning away a good chunk of the webs. It strikes the spider, melting part of its carapace and enraging it further. Ash has given it a priority target, and the thing leaps at him, sinking fangs into his arm. The obrimos screams and falls to his knees as he feels it injecting something into him--this monster is venomous.<br /> <br /> A second later, Midas's sword cuts through the spider's body, finishing the job and cleaving the monster in two. Kismet immediately jumps to attending Ash, having invested in the Life Arcanum. She heals his wound and, when he states he feels wrong, she attempts to purify the poison. This doesn't work as well as either of them like.<br /> <br /> Blackness begins to pour from Ash's eyes, nose, ears, and mouth, and Midas and Kismet realize from how that horrid fountain wriggles and squirms that it's not ichor--it's more spiders! The monster spirit-spider's venom was even more spiders. It takes a moment for it to end and for the dregs to skitter away into the darkness, leaving Ash pale and shivering from the disgusting and unexpected horror he'd just experienced. Midas and Kismet help him to his feet, saying nothing as he shivers in their hold, and help guide him further into the temple.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> This was the first session and the one we got the most wrong. There was no rhyme or reason to the gathering or the venture beyond the fact that they were all mages, they were part of a secret society, and clearly this is what secret societies do. A pointless party was held in the woods and the council hands off a quest to the newbies. There are other issues, which you may have noticed already, and I'll be elaborating on those in the next installment.<br /> <br /> I adjusted and this was adjusted canonically as we went forward, but there's only so much you can do for damage control on a gaffe this large. The gathering was now incidental, there were behind-the-scenes rumblings involving certain individuals which will be elaborated on later, and there's something of a reasoning behind it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 04-09-2017, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T13:45:15-07:00","id":1075580,"title":"","content":"It's weird how &quot;Vomiting spiders from his eyes&quot; is nostalgic for me these days. It's one of the few things <i>not</i> regrettable about this bit.<br /> <br /> This whole arc and the breakdowns that followed were one big lesson in &quot;Learn what your players want and don't just expect the characters to mesh together&quot;. It should've been a big warning sign from the get-go that all the players were really, <i>really</i> after different things, given how they reacted.<br /> <br /> Also, a big reason for why setting guides that help you think about how a given society runs are a good idea.<br /> <br /> Worth adding to this that the entire temple was meant to be the skeletal remains of an enormous snake god. Don't ask me why. Another good thing: Planning symbolism before spectacle.<br /> <br /> Don't mind me, folks, I'm just adding the Director's Commentary to this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:14:19-07:00","id":1076103,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Chapter 1: Blood and Spiders<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Part 2</span></span><br /> <br /> Eventually, Ash gets his bearings and manages to walk on his own again, They journey takes them deeper, past smoother rocks which look organically-carved, and finally they exit into a large chamber. There's a large cylinder before them, and in front of that is an altar. It's flanked on each side by stone jaguars, and from the grooves in it and the way they drain into a pattern around the cylinder, it's not hard to tell just what sort of chamber this is: the ritual sacrifice, drain-the-blood kind. There are no other exits out of the chamber than the way they entered, and this is the only path they took which hadn't ended in an empty room, so the cabal concludes that this place must have whatever it was Orcus was looking for--that, or he wanted the giant spider, and the ship had already sailed on that one.</span><br /> <br /> They approach the altar, and it's not hard for them to figure things out, even with mage sight: the stone cylinder is tied to the blood-draining mechanisms, as the carvings across its surface depicts a man in a mask holding aloft what is likely a heart above an altar, as others before it bow. From the way the stone jaguars shimmer in their sights, though, it's easy to tell it won't be as simple as a little bloodletting. Since Kismet knows enough of Life to heal, they elect to cut themselves and cheat the ritual. Ash is given the option to abstain, given he just dealt with spider-poison, but as they perform the act it becomes clear they're going to risk exhausting Kismet's mana or bleeding themselves to dangerous points, so Ash eventually chips in.<br /> <br /> Of course, the stone jaguars don't appreciate the ritual being cheated like this, and very quickly become not-stone jaguars. Just as quickly, however, the three mages put them down, leaving them as shattered remnants on the floor.<br /> <br /> The three of them stand there for a while, wrists open over the grooves in the stonework, until finally they hear the sound of stone scraping against stone. Kismet runs her fingers across their wounds, and their cuts close. The cylinder rotates and the front of it falls away, revealing its contents. There are some weapons on racks, vaguely resembling but not placeable as belonging to several mesoamerican civilizations of the past, none of them registering as magical in their eyes, but the clear prize is sitting on a pedestal in the center of it all. It's a golden mask, and from its shape it's obviously the one depicted on the stone carvings.<br /> <br /> Having dealt with stone jaguars, a giant spider, and ritual bloodletting, they carefully take the mask from its resting place and hightail it out of the temple as fast as they can. It feels strange in Ash's grip, like it's made of something which neither absorbs or radiates heat. Outside, as they wait for Marx to open a portal back home, they finally get the chance to socialize. Kismet's reserved but friendly, Midas is all smiles and easy to converse with. Standing out is Ash, who almost seems traumatized by the experience; he's quiet, staring off into nothing, and when he's finally drawn out of that state all they can really get out of him is that this wasn't what he expected at all going into all of this.<br /> <br /> The portal opens, and the now-proven mages are shuffled back in front of the councilors. Midas passes the mask to Orcus, and even though the old mystagogue's eyes are hidden by his hood it's easy to tell he's happy--not at getting the mask, but that it was this team that did it, as if it proved some small thing to him. To the side, Adelaide watches, still smiling. Orcus praises them, and it comes time for them to speak. Kismet goes first, and her words are a short expression of thanks. Midas is much the same, though more eloquent and with overtures on being pleased to add to the Mysterium's storehouse.<br /> <br /> Then it's Ash's turn.<br /> <br /> &quot;What the <i>fuck</i> did you have us do?&quot;<br /> <br /> The obrimos isn't happy with what's occurred. They treaded haphazardly through an untouched site, smashing stone statues that were possibly thousands of year old, disturbing mechanism worth studying, and killing a- okay, he can't be too upset that the spider died, but maybe killing it wasn't the best option. And for what? A stupid mask? They should've sent a team, they should've sent an archaeologist, they should've sent anyone but three newbies with no experience in any relevant fields.<br /> <br /> Some of the councilors look unhappy with this turn of events--they clearly weren't on board with this venture, but it's another to be challenged so openly and brazenly. Seshat, especially, looks upset. Adelaide to the side looks horrified. Goch looks somewhere between mortified and furious, mouth hanging open and eyes blazing at the audacity of his mentee.<br /> <br /> Orcus, for his part, takes it in stride, likely having expected it. He assures Ash that sometimes there's reason and meaning behind events like this, that it's worth trusting in the words and judgment of your wisers.<br /> <br /> &quot;You move in mysterious ways?&quot; Ash prods. That earns a sharp frown from Orcus. Marx, meanwhile, is beaming at the whole display, having managed to catch herself in the middle of the beginning of a clap before realizing that probably wouldn't help matters.<br /> <br /> Things conclude quickly after that. Their meeting adjourns and everyone begins to leave. Orcus is disappointed but not entirely crestfallen, and before he goes he pats Ash on the shoulder in a conciliatory gesture, vowing that they'll talk later. Goch stares at Ash with fury, and with all the grace of a husband disappointed by their drunken spouse or a parent angry at the very public tantrum their child just threw, said he'd be pulling the car around and waiting.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zBz_56nG5Qg\" target=\"_blank\">Ash stands on the edge of the clearing, watching everyone mingle as the impromptu festivities start to end. Midas and Kismet are clustered near Adelaide. They're wearing smiles, exchanging pleasant words. Midas cranes his neck to look for him, and when he finally does he gestures for Ash to join them. Ash raises a hand in refusal, but meets it with a forced smile--something about it would be wrong, with the way Midas is glowing from all the positive attention. Guests file past, thanking Adelaide, and it's easy to tell just who let the word out. Marx is halfway through a portal to god-knows-where when he catches her gaze, and surprisingly she offers him a small wink--a subtle mark of attention that leaves him a little startled.<br /> <br /> Ash's tearducts still tingle, and he still tastes foul hairs on his tongue. There's a black streak leftover from the adventure down the white dress shirt he's wearing. A breeze picks up, chilling the moist stain. He turns to follow Goch, sparing a final look at Adelaide and what he supposes is now his cabal. Kismet and Midas's backs are to him, but Adelaide is now crouching, stroking the back of a fox that even from here Ash can tell is more than what it appears--probably a familiar, like the spirit hound Midas had told him about. Her eyes briefly meet his, and there's no anger or disappointment in them; they're focused, searching for something in the way he looks back.<br /> <br /> He vanishes into the woods.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> The big problem here is that the Mysterium actually does have things like what Ash described, and does what Ash says should've been done. This was a clumsy smash-and-grab on what might as well have been a mage heritage site, and there's no real way to get around that this makes no sense.<br /> <br /> As time went on there came to be a reason behind this--this was a test, something was being looked for in all of this, and it might not've just been the mask they found. It was the only way to squeeze an ounce of sense out the mistakes that we made in the process of this first chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 04-10-2017, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T18:32:06-07:00","id":1076228,"title":"","content":"How large is atypically large for a consilium? Say 30 mages altogether?<br /> I appreciate how DnDish your opening was x3, the first game I was in was about to go that way too but it died before it even started because two players immediately started drama that got so bad it started tension in a completely different game at a different meet-up.<br /> Looking forward to who this Frank is...<br /> Ash sounds interesting, I'm glad he called Orcus out on this event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T21:22:00-07:00","id":1076281,"title":"","content":"It was about 200, actually. It was really ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Since then, I have gone back and revised the setting heavily. It has a setting Mystery, and the previously incredibly dense Mage population has been spread across an entire state. More justifications added, more tweaked to give it a theme of its own, and more reason for Mages to be there than the ST really liking the Pacific rainforest.<br /> <br /> None of that happened during this arc, though. The entire tenure of the Three-Headed Dragon, it's one big, blobby, flavourless mass, which definitely did not help things. Ash's anti-mystical side probably got no small helping from me just not knowing how to actually make for effective mysticism.<br /> <br /> Honestly, his hard reductionist stance always rankled with me too. It took away from a lot of what I liked about the setting, even if I had no idea how to effectively wield or implement it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T05:43:10-07:00","id":1076424,"title":"","content":"Ash growing out of that ended up being a large part of his arc at the end of the first and during the entirety of the second chronicle, in case anyone is worried about that.<br /> <br /> This said, Ash's understanding of how this whole &quot;magic&quot; thing works parallels my own coming to comprehend it. In the first sessions, I think during one especially-heated discussion on how much of a bullheaded idiot Ash was about it, I ended up trying to summarize his views as some sort of weird unitarian thing where he'd be the kind of guy to write the M:tA corebook.<br /> <br /> That was a ridiculous thing; not only did he and I not really comprehend that Mages don't really believe that they're, say, conjuring fire from hell and instead view that as a lens to come closer to the absolute Truth of conjuring fire, but he genuinely believed the way he was doing it was the only way (and in one of the few instances of me 'getting' it, I knew and intended for him to be absolutely wrong on that point).<br /> <br /> In my defense, we hadn't begun looking at later books of Mage 1E yet, and so we were pulling from the earliest books of 1E. The magic presented then was far more hermetic than gnostic, and I'm glad that's changed going into 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 04-11-2017, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T14:45:57-07:00","id":1076664,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Interlude I: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7tMFs-5FlWk\" target=\"_blank\">Heroin</a>e</b></span><br /> <br /> When Ash stepped into this wider world, he was confident that it\u2019d be filled with people of high ideals and meaning, but since then he\u2019s seen that just as many of his new peers are capable of short-sighted stupidity, selfishness, and blind arrogance. Goch certainly hasn\u2019t improved those perceptions, with the way he\u2019s been avoiding speaking with Ash like an upset parent. The heady sense of optimism\u2014hell, the feeling of being rescued\u2014has begun to tarnish. Everything is different, but it\u2019s looking the same as it ever was. He lives like a ghost, without a job, without friends, and without a former life worth clinging to.<br /> <br /> The next time Ash takes a walk through Portland, Marx is waiting for him. She\u2019s right around a corner, like she\u2019d expected him. Like she\u2019d been waiting for him. It doesn\u2019t take much to sway him, a few nice words, a few remarks on how impressed she and her friends are, and suddenly Ash finds himself with her arm over his shoulders and him being guided into a nearby bar. He\u2019s never had much attention, especially from the opposite sex, and he\u2019s caught too off-guard to even consider not following her lead.<br /> <br /> Having been dry his entire life, it\u2019s not in Ash\u2019s character to ask for a drink. Having never been surrounded by people proud of and praising him either, and that makes it impossible to resist the frothing mug that\u2019s pushed in front of his fact. It tastes terrible on his tongue, but their looks are expectant and his need to push something, anything right now spurs him on. He\u2019s not sure what it is, but it hits him fast, making his face warm and his joints lose.<br /> <br /> More importantly, it\u2019s easier to not think about where he is, and why he is, and what it all means. For the moment, it just is, and there\u2019s a heavyset man clapping him on the back, while Marx glows like a saint, backlit by some neon jukebox straight out of the 1960s. When she smiles, he can\u2019t help but do the same.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not infatuation, he\u2019s positive. He\u2019s felt that before. This runs deeper, something more meaningful. Gratitude, he fails to think the word. A drowning man being thrown a lifejacket he hadn\u2019t even known he\u2019d needed, and right now he owes that to her. Emboldened, they feed him more drinks and he keeps downing them. The relief is so great he nearly cries. The openness and invincibility is so atypical he worries that there may be something wrong, but it\u2019s hard to think that for long, not when he\u2019s suddenly dragged into a game of quarters. It\u2019s like they knew he\u2019s use his magic to cheat.<br /> <br /> Time vanishes. Most of the group has cleared out, and Ash realizes he never asked their names\u2014that he didn\u2019t even want to know. Things are dying down, and he\u2019s struggling to remember when things started up enough for that to begin happening. They move to the run down apartment of one of the group, a guy he overhears Marx talking to enough to catch the name \u201cCharlie.\u201d<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s3hzOZL38m4\" target=\"_blank\">Charlie is turning water into cocaine</a> when Ash realizes there\u2019s a drug lab in the corner. Marx is smoking something, and when she catches him staring she holds it out.<br /> <br /> \u201cTry this,\u201d she commands.<br /> <br /> He can\u2019t find it in himself to deny it. Not on this night, not with the things he\u2019s already done, not from the woman who gave him this. He takes it, and (after clumsily being walked through how to inhale) his lungs take a blow and suddenly that pleasant numbness he\u2019s been walking with metastasizes into a floating euphoria. He laughs. She laughs. He hugs her, and she returns it after several seconds.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the early morning when Marx tears a portal back to the outskirts of Goch\u2019s mansion and leads him through, a back full of\u2026 whatever it is he\u2019d smoked stuffed into a pants pocket and a phone number written on a piece of paper covered In chemical formulas in his hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you want more, call this,\u201d she tells him. \u201cIf things get too weird, we\u2019ll make it stop, too,\u201d she offers. He doesn\u2019t want it to stop. And if things were to go south, he couldn\u2019t imagine asking them to fix things\u2014not when he could call on Kismet to clean his blood or brain instead.<br /> <br /> A few days later, hanging with Charlie and a few other non-faces, Ash allows himself to try a few pills, one\u2019s he told are safe to mix. Two weeks later, he tries a bit of white powder they\u2019re in the middle of snorting. A month goes by, and he lets them show him how to tie off a vein. Marx\u2019s smile is wide and the fist-bumps he receives from the others are hard enough to bruise, once he does it right himself. By the second month he\u2019s no longer stumbling into situations and being offered advice, he\u2019s asking them directly if they have anything new.<br /> <br /> Ash knows it\u2019s dangerous, and risky, and wrong. But that ship\u2019s sailed, hasn\u2019t it? Everything he already knew is wrong, everything that he\u2019d hoped for is wrong, so why wouldn\u2019t this be right? Why can\u2019t it be? It helps him think, it helps him sleep, it makes him feel ways he\u2019s never felt before, and, after all, magic keeps it from having any lasting effects, so they\u2019re being responsible.<br /> <br /> Years later, when he stops to think about it, he\u2019ll realize Marx was trying to poach him, probably in hopes that influence over him might extend into influence over Orcus. He\u2019ll also realize she succeeded\u2014he wouldn\u2019t betray his Order, but any position she took he would\u2019ve echoed, and anything she wanted to do he would've supported. He\u2019ll also realize he didn\u2019t mind it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> EDIT: Replaced the old story to something that flows better. Also incorporates a bit of my own experiences in using substances to treat depression, which definitely requires this emphasis: <b>it's a bad idea, unless they've been prescribed.</b> It's easy to make excuses and justifications to yourself and have them make sense at the time. There will be a lot of that with Ash.<br /> <br /> This was possibly our biggest retcon, as it didn't come until well into the second chronicle. Ash is an addict, mostly as a result of the sudden wave of depression that hits him on realizing becoming a Mage doesn't make you or anyone else a better person, and needing an outlet to cope with the fact that he hadn't escaped so many of the things which made his former life so empty.<br /> <br /> In-game, this was reflected as him just showing up as user one day out of the blue, shooting heroin and snorting coke and drinking tons. It was only later than I bothered asking &quot;where, why, and how.&quot; Marx was the obvious answer, as in-game she and her friends were his major source of substances and also his major source of social entertainment. He also tended to work with Marx more frequently than others.<br /> <br /> What isn't a retcon is Charlie: he was canonically Ash's major source of drugs, an associate of Marx, and a recurring mute background character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 04-11-2017, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:31:27-07:00","id":1077388,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Interlude II: Pathos</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The sun is going down through the window of Ash's spartan guestroom, and he is abruptly startled awake from a nap. He's been sleeping better since developing his vices, and he's been left more tired than usual with his late-night activities with Marx and her buddies. Despite this, </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">the sleep he has been getting has only become more restless, plagued by strange dreams which feel almost as vivid as reality but still leave him struggling to hold onto their meanings once he's awake again. When they're gone, they leave behind a sense of intense, uncertain urgency which drives him crazy. So is the case this time.<br /> <br /> Ash leans over to his nightstand and hurriedly pulls out what's in it: a copy of the christian bible and a phonebook. The dreams have left a passage behind that he remembers, and he hurriedly finds the verse. Compulsively, he flips to a page in the yellow pages which corresponds to the verse, and is met with a full-page ad for a nightclub he'd driven past once or twice. For a second, he freezes, wondering what the hell he's doing, thinking about how this makes no sense.<br /> <br /> &quot;Nothing better to do,&quot; he affirms to himself. He pushes the books away and heads out the door.</span></span><br /> <br /> By the time Ash has found a parking spot and walked to the club, it's dark. The place is a small-scale operation, as evidenced by it mostly being one room of modest size with a bar on one end, a stage on the other, and seating throughout the rest. A woman dressed up as a stereotypical stage magician is performing on stage at the moment, and Ash takes a seat at the bar to watch. Boredly, he decides to read the auras of the guests, and notices that the magician is the only one who lights up so bright.<br /> <br /> She's one of the Awakened. He's feeling less skeptical about those strange dreams now, even as he's trying to convince himself that this is still more than likely a coincidence.<br /> <br /> Ash sticks around and watches the show, only having two shots of... honestly he didn't ask the bartender. No sense in getting sloshed right now, he wants to stay clearheaded for this. About ten minutes after the magician's set, she shows up at the bar in plainclothes, asking the bartender for a drink. Ash determines that he should talk to her. Not because of any mysterious dreams, of course, just, y'know, to make conversation. He's only doing it because he wants to, of course. He looks over, and attempts to subtly start a conversation about their shared nature.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, what Order?&quot; Ash asks, not even looking at her. Swing and a miss.<br /> <br /> The woman turns to look at Ash, and gives him a long, cautious look. He's done something similar enough to know she's examining him like he'd done earlier. Finally, she replies. &quot;Not here,&quot; she says, and Ash finds himself being pulled into the club's small unisex bathroom. &quot;Spill,&quot; she orders.<br /> <br /> Ash holds up his hands defensively. &quot;Argentum Everto, Silver Ladder. I was stopping in on a walk for some drinks and there you were.&quot; It's not <i>really</i> a lie, and it was far less suspect than 'my dreams led me to you.' Which they certainly didn't. &quot;I saw you and thought it'd be worth saying hello.&quot;<br /> <br /> The woman scrutinizes him for a moment more, then extends her hand. &quot;Pathos. Silver Ladder,&quot; she says as Ash shakes her hand.<br /> <br /> Their conversation is brief--after all, they are having it in a public place in a room usually intended for only one person, but it's amicable. She's trying to inspire some wonder and curiosity through stage magic--not the most original trick, but it's hers and she's good at it. Ash shares his feelings of being the odd-man-out and is entirely honest when he says he'd like to work with her--it's a thing to do, finally, and there's no baggage associated with her like there is Goch or his cabal or the consilium.<br /> <br /> &quot;Remember, if anyone asks, I was the best you'd ever had,&quot; he jokes as she moves to open the door. He hadn't even realized he'd been making the joke until it was out of his mouth; it's uncharacteristically daring.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aENX1Sf3fgQ\" target=\"_blank\">Pathos gives him a funny look, but smiles. &quot;Oh yeah, you rocked my world,&quot; she returns, turning the door handle.<br /> <br /> ~ ~ ~<br /> <br /> When Ash finally leaves the club, more tipsy than he'd entered it, he's feeling optimistic again. Sure, the first few months have been a series of disappointments, but he's finding himself capable of things he'd never thought of before, doing things he's never considered. Plus he'll be performing as Dr. Science in a few weeks, once he figures out a direction for the set--he's thinking prop-comedy interspersed with educational punchlines, but it's still a work in progress.<br /> <br /> Maybe just because he's been handed more of the same problems doesn't mean he can't make something of them. Maybe he has the right tools, the right friends to make a meaning for himself this time around.<br /> <br /> He'll feel a bit silly the day he eventually goes up on stage in a frizzy white wig and waves around a plasma pistol which would comically and mysteriously misfire, but afterwards, when he and Pathos discuss their acts and how to improve them with each other, he can't feel it is anything but the best decision he's made in a while.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> These were the early games, where things were looking up. But you've all presumably read the title.<br /> <br /> So I left it out, but interludes were regularly hosted for each individual player. They were brief scenes, mostly to elaborate on or establish elements relevant to those characters or the story at large. This one more or less happened exactly as described.<br /> <br /> The focus of this interlude was Ash's dreams. Ash had the Dream merit, and as the game went on it became stronger as I bought it up to max. Naturally, at the early stages, getting insight and advice from cryptic moments in the middle of meditation and REM sleep didn't mesh well with a man who had spent his life believing in empirical evidence and Occam's razor.<br /> <br /> He also had the Eidetic Memory merit, and that got used a lot in conversations and in references, mostly for the sake of him being a smug asshole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 04-12-2017, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T11:33:08-07:00","id":1078979,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Interlude III: Goch</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;You don't know how?&quot; Pathos asks one night over dinner. Their sets are done, and the place has mostly cleared out. They're splitting a bag of stale chips and some unfinished complementary bread as the staff begins to turn over chairs and set them on tables.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm sitting there in what's left of the frame of my home, and he just drives up in a limo,&quot; Ash affirms. &quot;I thought you- I thought we had a spell or something that tells us.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No, Ash,&quot; Pathos says. &quot;Unless... he's not an Acanthus, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> Ash shakes his head.<br /> <br /> &quot;Not as likely, then.&quot; Pathos takes a bite out of her bread, and chews it thoughtfully. &quot;You need to ask. Or find out. It's not good with us for someone else to know more about what's going on with you than yourself.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ash grunts, taking another slice.<br /> <br /> ~ ~ ~</span></span><br /> <br /> It's the next morning when Ash approaches Goch at the table. He's sitting across from a mountain of a man named Volund, someone else that near as Ash can tell lives there too--they'd never been formally introduced, and had only caught his name on occasions when Goch had been speaking with the man. They both look expectantly at him; this is the first time they've seen him in the mornings in the past two months, and from the way his eyes are sunken Ash is certain they can tell he hasn't slept. His eyes are also bloodshot and his clothes wrinkled, so he's positive they can read the hangover.<br /> <br /> Silently, Ash takes a seat and a piece of grapefruit. After eating it, he asks: &quot;How did you find me?&quot;<br /> <br /> Volund freezes in the middle of raising a spoon of cereal to his mouth. Goch stiffens, and slowly puts down the paper he's been reading. He's smiling, and it's the opposite of reassuring.<br /> <br /> &quot;I was keeping track of you,&quot; Goch says, eyes much wider than they'd been a moment ago.<br /> <br /> Ash sits there for a moment, waiting for Goch to elaborate on that creepy statement. When Goch doesn't, Ash asks &quot;why?&quot; It comes out lower and drier than he wants.<br /> <br /> &quot;My family has,&quot; Goch elaborates. &quot;We've been following lots of people. For a while.&quot; He leans forward, and Ash instinctively leans back. &quot;You're part of a long, proud line, Argentum.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ash momentarily thinks back to his childhood, to dad's rough fists, to mom's backyard target practice on painted and overturned garbage cans, to mom being dragged away to police and ambulance sirens as some nameless officer places a blanket over his shoulders and sits with him.<br /> <br /> &quot;... are you sure about that?&quot; Ash asks.<br /> <br /> Goch nods. &quot;We've been taking care of you. I'm taking care of you.&quot; His breathing seems heavier. &quot;My father looked after your family.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ash is squirming his way to his feet. &quot;I don't think-&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Emerich,&quot; Goch says.<br /> <br /> Ash freezes, hand on the back of his seat. Uncle Emerich. Slowly, he eases himself back into his seat, though he keeps himself pressed into the back of it.<br /> <br /> &quot;We've been looking after you for generations. And here you are,&quot; Goch says. From the way Goch licks his lips, Ash expects a 'finally' has gone unspoken. &quot;You owe yourself to the Thule Society.&quot;<br /> <br /> It takes a moment for Ash to process what he's just heard, and he tries to remember where he's heard that name bef- oh. Oh shit. He goes rigid, and his dark-rimmed eyes go wide. The skin on his face tightens, and he puts on long-lipped look which would be at home on a befuddled frog.<br /> <br /> Goch seems oblivious to Ash's sudden shock, and immediately jumps to his feet. &quot;Here, let me show you something,&quot; he says, urging Ash to follow. Ash, numb inside in a way even Charlie's drugs couldn't replicate, stands and follows.<br /> <br /> They walk through the long halls of the mansion, up a few flights of stairs, past a row of portraits which Ash suddenly finds himself seeing in a new light. &quot;Honestly, I don't know why people treat eugenics like it's such a dirty word,&quot; Goch says. &quot;Sure, it's hard some formative issues and has been exploited, but it's a legitimate science.&quot; They stop before the door to the attic loft. He produces a key, and unlocks the door. &quot;I mean, it's not like we're Nazis.&quot; Goch opens the door.<br /> <br /> Ash is treated to the sight of filing cabinets, bins filled with organized and tagged files, and a dozen angry red swastika banners hanging from the walls.<br /> <br /> Goch is silent for a moment. &quot;I thought we took those down,&quot; he declares.<br /> <br /> The bottom falls out of Ash's stomach. He's had spiders crawl out of his ears and eyes, but somehow this is the most insane thing he's seen and heard since Awakening. The worst part is, it makes an element of sense--his mother's psychoses, his father's bitter resignation, uncle Emerich's strong kicks and german utterances. It's ridiculous. It's horrifying. This is part of the world he's a part of now? These people claimed membership and allegiance to the society of mages he belongs to now?<br /> <br /> Ash's jaw hangs open, and he looks at Goch. Dark-skinned Goch, who doesn't have a seperate bedroom set up for Volund. Ash tries to say something, but all that comes out of his mouth are giggles and laughs. There's too much monstrous absurdity right now to open that can of worms.<br /> <br /> Goch grins back nervously, and leads Ash into the room. He sits him down on a metal folding chair before a table of file-bins. &quot;Everything here, invoices, lineages, medical records, everything, back four to six generations.&quot; He's eager, and slides one bin in front of Ash. He recognizes the family name on it. The giggles have faded, leaving him numb save for an unsettling tickle in his chest. He pulls a file and pages through it, noticing names and dates, noting some people have lightning bolts marked next to their names.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q2zwgUhTIPI\" target=\"_blank\">There's a welling urge to set it all on fire, to put an end to this, to- to- to erase this bit of his history that makes him sick and delirious with disgust. All it'd take is one image to set it all going, to leave this abominable racist legacy in ash.<br /> <br /> &quot;Everything's here, and now you're here,&quot; Goch says over Ash's shoulder. And just like that, Ash hears that tone of desperation in Goch's voice. Ash turns his head to look at his mentor and host, at the wide smile on his features. Ash can see the man's childhood, can see the sorts of things Emerich undoubtably did to his emotions, to hear the sorts of things that were undoubtably said. But he can't comprehend the depths of the sort of damage Emerich had inflicted on his own son to make him the dutiful steward of everything against who he was. And he feels that, empathizes with it, sees lines and parallels between the two of them, fighting so hard to hold onto them through the simmering hatred he feels for everything this stands for and for those people who were stupid and monstrous and decadent enough to hold onto it over the decades.<br /> <br /> And like that, everything Ash is feeling drains away.<br /> <br /> &quot;Okay,&quot; Ash says, and it feels like vomiting. Calmly, he turns his attention back to his family's file, and blindly reaches for another bin, not caring who he pulls information on.<br /> <br /> Goch pats Ash on the shoulder. &quot;I'll have Volund fry some bacon,&quot; he offers.<br /> <br /> &quot;Alright,&quot; Ash says. &quot;I'll be here. Looking over this.&quot; Memorizing names. Remembering ledgers. Familiarizing himself with victims.<br /> <br /> &quot;So... please don't embarrass us again,&quot; Goch says at the doorframe.<br /> <br /> &quot;When you say us...&quot; Ash lets it hang as he opens a manilla envelope full of receipts.<br /> <br /> &quot;You and me,&quot; Goch replies.<br /> <br /> This gives Ash a moment of pause. &quot;... right.&quot;<br /> <br /> Goch smiles and closes the door behind him. Ash is left with a mountain of misdeeds. It's a nightmare. He's waited for an answer, desperately asked the universe for one as to why things in his life happened the way they did. It makes so much sense. His skin feels hot, but his insides feel cold. He and Goch never had a chance.<br /> <br /> Ash's chest quakes one in a single chuckle. He keeps reading.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> When I play in games I try to write plothooks for STs to hang stories or developments off of if they want to. I also make it clear that they're welcome to fit anything they'd like into any spot I'm not explicit about. In this case, I never clarified just how it was Ash's mentor found him beyond showing up at Ash's burned-out house.<br /> <br /> Of everything that could've filled in there, this was the last thing I expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 04-15-2017, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T13:23:34-07:00","id":1079021,"title":"","content":"You could say you did Nazi it coming?<br /> <br /> There's a lot I underutilized with Ash. There's history there not worth going into, but, if I knew then what I knew now, I might've tightened the focus. Made it more about him and Pathos and coming to terms with the idea that there is nothing in the world but what we make of it. That hell is other people and so is heaven, etc.<br /> <br /> The game went interesting places nonetheless, but who knows what it might've been?<br /> <br /> The Thule Society stuff was something I don't really remember the genesis of; why I used it and such. I regretted it, because it played further into Ash's constant loathing of Mages and Mage society, but the introduction and the complexity it added to Goch were fun, at the very least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","user":"Axelgear","date":". 04-15-2017, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-22T21:55:27-07:00","id":1082516,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Chapter 2: Ripper Man(?)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Part 1</b></span><br /> <br /> \u201c-for all you or anyone else knew, you could\u2019ve been inviting an incursion.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tartarus glares across the conference room at Ash. Ash is standing at a podium before the five seated councilors, and of them all only Marx looks particularly happy. Ash is wearing a rumpled suit, and is using sunglasses to obscure his bloodshot eyes\u2014but somehow, everyone can tell he\u2019s glaring right back. Midas and Kismet are off to each side, looking differing degrees of contrite.<br /> <br /> \u201cDisbelief is something worth testing the limits of. I believe-\u201c Ash begins.<br /> <br /> Tartarus interrupts. \u201cWhat you believe doesn\u2019t matter when everyone else has to pay the price for it!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut nobody did,\u201d Ash replies evenly.<br /> <br /> Before Tartarus and Ash can escalate this into a full-on shouting match, Orcus speaks up. \u201cThe two of you have very strong opinions, but neither of them are why we are here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tartarus glowers, but remains silent.<br /> <br /> Midas clears his throat and steps forward. \u201cI\u2026 think Ash\u2019s work was valid,\u201d he declares. The eyes o the entire room fall on him. \u201cWhat he\u2019s trying to do\u2014it\u2019s worth trying, isn\u2019t it? Done right and done well. He didn\u2019t force us to do anything. I did it because I wanted to.\u201d<br /> <br /> Orcus gives Midas a small smile. \u201cYes, but this was his idea, and his plan. And, as he pointed out, nobody suffered for it. Bad judgment isn\u2019t the same as reckless endangerment.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd we only need to make one example,\u201d Tartarus provides.<br /> <br /> \u201cAsh,\u201d Orcus says, \u201cwhat you did, and made your cabal party to, was dangerous and reckless. Now, you were right.\u201d At that, Ash glows with smugness. \u201cIf you weren\u2019t,\u201d Orcus continues, sounding all the world like a parent trying to make a child understand why spilling a drink is bad, \u201cthis would be a different conversation. You risked yourself, your cabal, and all those Sleepers. We are here to try and give you a picture of the seriousness of your actions, and to determine whether further steps should be taken in this\u2026 unusual case.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI get it,\u201d Ash says, voice dripping with irritation. \u201cI went too far, fine. I\u2019ll dial it back.\u201d<br /> <br /> Orcus looks momentarily relieved, but then Tartarus speaks. \u201cYou\u2019ll stop it,\u201d the Guardian declares.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re done,\u201d Orcus speaks before commentary can break down further. \u201cI propose a vote. All not in favor of censuring Argentum Everto?\u201d<br /> <br /> Marx immediately throws up her hand. After a moment\u2019s hesitation, Seshat follows. Orcus glances over at Dagda, ignoring Tartarus\u2014his stance is obvious enough. Dagda keeps his hand down.<br /> <br /> With a sigh, Orcus raises his own hand.<br /> <br /> Ash grins sharply, looking at Tartarus. Tartarus snorts. \u201cIf you\u2019re here again, things will go differently, Argentum. Remember that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Orcus sighs. \u201cYes, they will,\u201d he says, and while Ash can\u2019t see the mystagogue\u2019s eyes under his hood, he can still feel the old man\u2019s pleading gaze.<br /> <br /> \u201cNoted,\u201d Ash says crisply.<br /> <br /> As the council disperses and the cabal leaves the conference room, Ash and Kismet find their shoulders clapped in Tartarus\u2019s iron grip. His gaze is stern. \u201cI know what you\u2019re made of,\u201d he says to Kismet, \u201cso I don\u2019t need to make a case for you. But you-\u201c he turns his gaze to Ash \u201c-probably need some emphasis.<br /> <br /> \u201cTwo of my associates are tracking and mopping up after some hellbeast we call the Ripper. It\u2019s been making gory messes across the state the past few months. There's something I desperately-&quot; Tartarus emphasizes the word &quot;-need to pursue, so I need some sets of able hands to help them take care of this one. I know a third of you is trustworthy, a third of you is competent, and a third of you-\u201c Tartarus\u2019s gaze settles on Ash. There\u2019s a moment of quiet. \u201c-If he cares enough about people enough to put them in danger for their own benefit, probably cares enough to try and save them if given the chance.\u201d<br /> <br /> The grip on Ash\u2019s shoulder tightens, and then lets go. Ash squirms away violently.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes sir,\u201d Kismet answers for them, stiffly. Ash shoots a sidelong glare at her, and then another to Tartarus. He\u2019s heard the rundown on their order from Goch, and he hasn\u2019t liked much of it.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhatever, death-squad buddies,\u201d Ash says, disappointed at the lack of rise it gets out of Tartarus. \u201cJust tell us where to go.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> Sorry this took so long to get out. Finals are coming up, and prep ate most of my time, along with a lovely family visit/vacation. I'll be trying to resume a one-a-day schedule, but until finals are done that's not a guarantee.<br /> <br /> The thing Ash is on trial for is left vague here because what he originally was up for in-game is something that would have summoned a gulmoth which would've probably killed a lot of people, as per 1E's rules on Paradox and Sleeper witnesses and so on. Bad things would've still happened in 2E, but not the same level of bad.<br /> <br /> In the original game, Ash and his cabal simulated <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ws6AAhTw7RA\" target=\"_blank\">quantum levitation</a> with selective applications of Forces at a science convention. This was before any of us were really fully aware on how Paradox and Disbelief interacted (and honestly Disbelief these days is still a little iffy--though I suspect that's deliberate). In 1E, it didn't really matter how Ash was dressing it up--the spells used were Obvious, and any Sleepers witnessing them, regardless of context, would invoke more Paradox.<br /> <br /> 2E, entertainingly, allows more wiggle-room in that regard, having done away with the idea of spells specifically being Obvious or Subtle, and in explicitly requiring Sleepers to be &quot;conscious and cognizant of the magic's impossibility.&quot; I still omitted it here, though, as what was done isn't as important as why and what followed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 04-23-2017, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T20:51:58-07:00","id":1082887,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\">Chapter 2: Ripper Man(?)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Part 2</span><br /> <br /> \u201cAll I\u2019m saying is Tartarus probably sent us on this to try and get me killed,\u201d Ash remarks as he wipes powder from his nose. \u201cGuy has it out for me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI wonder why?\u201d Kismet \u2018asks.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, you would take his side despite going along with it all, wouldn\u2019t you?\u201d Ash grouses before taking a swig from a flask.<br /> <br /> The elevator they\u2019re riding dings and opens, and the cabal exits into the grungy hallway of the third floor of an apartment building. As they reach the studio apartment Tartarus had told them about, it\u2019s hard not to notice the faint red stains just beneath the door.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhoah, what\u2019s with all the-\u201c Midas opens the door to the studio apartment, revealing a place splattered in red, with a body pinned to the wall that\u2019s been cut open from crotch to sternum \u201c-blood,\u201d Ash finishes after a second\u2019s pause. He reaches into a pocket, to the small pouch of powder there, and takes another snort.<br /> <br /> There are two mages already present, both dressed far too professionally for the work they are doing, as the blood-splatters on their clothing show. They give the simple lowdown: they\u2019ve been following the Ripper, mostly through an unreliable combination of precognition and resonance-tracking, but somehow the two things keep ending up running them in the wrong directions as much as the right.<br /> <br /> Midas and Ash are offering their own perspectives on it when Kismet speaks up. \u201cHe\u2019s still alive,\u201d she says.<br /> <br /> Everyone in the room immediately stops talking, and shares a series of horrified looks. The body isn\u2019t breathing. The clearly-visible organs aren\u2019t pumping, but at the same time, they now notice, pallor isn\u2019t draining from the \u2018dead\u2019 man\u2019s face, and his eyes haven\u2019t gone glassy in their frozen stare of horror. The man isn\u2019t there, his soul is also gone, but somehow those connections still remain.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think I can\u2026\u201d Kismet trails off as she sets a hand on the victim\u2019s forehead, her eyes suddenly focusing on something far in the distance, trying to follow everything that man is missing to the source. Her mind trails into the gaping chest cavity, into the empty non-spot his essential spark would\u2019ve been, until suddenly\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026it comes out the other side. The landscape is protean. The skyline is a mess of strange buildings and odd landscape formations, cascading from one into another with a strange transparency effect. The skies themselves are empty, a blackness that the horizon seems to be bleeding into, evaporating into.<br /> <br /> At the edge of everything on the verge of the abyss, is a pillar of pale green light. It bends perspective\u2014it doesn\u2019t change size in Kismet\u2019s view even as her perceptions get close to it, going from a thick thing dominating a chunk of the horizon to a column a little wider than a person, and it stretches so high into the darkness that it seems to bend overhead when looking up at it. Around it stand four people in green cloaks. In the hands of one is a ball of shifting light. The cloaked person squeezes, and massages, and it distorts and grows into the shape of a man\u2014the same man, Kismet\u2019s recognizes, that\u2019s sitting torn-open.<br /> <br /> The other cloaked figures place their hands on the soul-shape of the not-dead man, and he flails ineffectually in their grasp. \u201cWhere am I?\u201d he screams. \u201cIs this hell?!\u201d As if in response, something inside the pillar strains, human outlines pressing against the insides of that shifting light, and Kismet realizes just where the undulations on its surface are coming from, and starts seeing it all: the skull-like screaming faces in it, the arms stretching out from it, only to be reabsorbed into the mass. And as she watches, the soul-shape is pressed into it and is pulled into it, howling in terror, by a score of desperate, grasping hands.<br /> <br /> The leader who\u2019d been handling the soul-shape\u2014or who she assumed was the leader, based on the intricate golden filigree on the robe\u2019s cuffs and hems\u2014dusts their hands off. \u201cGood work,\u201d he tells his associates in a deep, masculine voice. &quot;Especially you, Miwok,&quot; he says to one who clinks when they move.<br /> <br /> The leader suddenly freezes \u201cThat\u2019s\u2026 familiar,\u201d He remarks to himself. The other three figures turn to look at him, and Kismet sees their faces: two women, one man. One of the women has chains around her face--Miwok. \u201cNot since\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Slowly, the leader turns, and Kismet sees his face. Young, handsome. Sharp features. An ashen-grey color to his skin, like a corpse. His eyes are a deep, unnatural green, and as they turn towards where Kismet is viewing, she sees them begin to blaze, sockets dimming as pinpricks of green fire begin to burn in them. His mouth hangs open in shock for a moment, and there\u2019s no doubt in Kismet\u2019s mind that he\u2019s looking directly at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cAfter all this time,\u201d the man says, lifting a hand to reach for her. Instantly his expression goes wild, and his mouth twists into a thin rictus grin. \u201cFound you.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 04-24-2017, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T22:39:18-07:00","id":1083858,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Chapter 2: Ripper Man(?)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Part 3</span><br /> <br /> The blackness of those eyes expands further, drawing Kismet in, until all the universe is just those two small green fires. \u201cCome back to me,\u201d she hears \u201cCome to Malthus.\u201d She\u2019s drifting deeper, and there\u2019s a pressure in her chest, a light guttering out, and then-<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s enough of that!\u201d Ash\u2019s voice cuts through it all.<br /> <br /> The world snaps back, and she\u2019s falling away, falling out of that darkness, and before the hellscape around her vanishes into the distance she sees the face of the leader\u2014Malthus\u2014twisted in fury. When Kismet comes back to herself, she\u2019s on her back in the apartment, suddenly gasping for air. It feels like somebody has snapped on her diaphragm like a rubber band. \u201cWha-\u201c is all she makes out before falling into a coughing fit.<br /> <br /> \u201cI broke the connection,\u201d Kismet hears Ash say. Midas kneels over her, looking apologetic, and adds \u201cAnd I sorta\u2026 punched your soul back in place.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd we need to get the fuck out of here,\u201d Ash remarks. The two Guardians are already prepping to leave, casting spells to wipe away the blood and the evidence. \u201cCall went out to the PD a second ago\u2014the second your chest began lighting up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFlatterer,\u201d Kismet dryly remarks as she gets back to her feet, rubbing her throat. Ash rolls his eyes, and stalks towards the door.<br /> <br /> Ash can already hear the sirens approaching by the time they hit the narrow alley through the fire escape, his skill over Forces carrying further than the doppler effect would normally allow. He stifles the sudden urge to giggle at how utterly insane what just happened was.<br /> <br /> \u201cHell of a series of events, right?\u201d Ash remarks over his shoulder to Midas and Kismet. He says it just in time for the manhole cover he\u2019s walking over to blow open and send him sprawling to the ground. It sends a gout of steam into the air which quickly fills the alley, refusing to disperse properly. He\u2019s already scrambling when he hits the ground, pulling himself up on his elbows and glancing frantically up and down.<br /> <br /> They all spot it at the same time. Its skin ripples, adopting a kaleidoscope of colors and tones, and there\u2019s the distinctive sensation from the way its body seems to undulate in place that the form it\u2019s currently wearing is temporary. For the moment though, it\u2019s noticeably feminine. The thing is nude, and its arms and legs are bending at the elbow, making it cling to one of the alley walls. The sunken eyes, the wild hair, and its current pose scream \u2018Exorcist.\u2019<br /> <br /> Dumbstruck, Ash yells the first thing that comes to mind: \u201cIs it weird I feel this is kinda hot?!\u201d<br /> <br /> Despite his sexual confusion, it\u2019s not hard to decide on a course of action. Immediately, Ash draws Winona\u2014his pistol\u2014and fires. The bullet catches the Ripper in the stomach. All that does it make it angry, and to his special sight he can see the beginnings of what must be an imago. He braces himself for what pain might come, and\u2026<br /> <br /> Ash\u2019s clothes fall empty around a chicken. It looks around, then begins to run and flail in panic. The thing\u2014the Ripper\u2014leaps.<br /> <br /> Midas reacts more smartly. He raises an arm and clasps his hands together, and a small geyser of sewer-water pulls itself from the open manhole. It and the steam condense around the Ripper, forming into a cocoon. The cocoon hardens into a dense, reddish-orange powder, entombing the Ripper in a packed shell of capsaicin.<br /> <br /> The effort, which creative, only slows the monster down for a second. It bursts from the powder like someone who\u2019d been buried in the sand, skin a burning red and pulsing, and makes for the Moros. Somehow, though, its feet and hands (which are now feet-hands), stumble over each other, and the Ripper goes careering face-first into the side of a dumpster. Kismet glares at it, hands in the form of a mudra.<br /> <br /> This distraction is enough to break its concentration, and suddenly Argentum Everto is back in the alley, naked and very shaken up. \u201cI am a Nazi chicken!\u201d he yells out. Even still collecting his wits, he instinctively rolls and grabs Winona from his pile of clothes, and this time when he pulls the trigger fire explodes from the barrel, lighting the Ripper on fire.<br /> <br /> The Ripper screeches, gouging chunks of metal off the dumpster as it rights itself. Its head turns independently of its shoulders, and its sunken eyes glare murder at the cabal. Despite this, it dives for the manhole, its pulsing form beginning to suppurate in places, and its head still on fire. The monster vanishes beneath the street, leaving the three mages confused and concerned.<br /> <br /> As they have a change to collect themselves, the cabal hears what it is they\u2019d forgotten all about in the scuffle: the police sirens. Ash scoops up his clothes and sprints for the edge of the alley. The light around him shimmers, bending until he\u2019s no longer visible.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll run ahead!\u201d Ash yells behind as the other two mages run for the opposite exit of the alley. \u201cI\u2019ll tell Tartarus!\u201d he promises, streaking naked and unseen through the city streets.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The name of Ash's gun is a reference to old Sci-Fi Channel show <i>Farscape.</i> It was originally named such as a joke, but it stuck. It's worth mentioning for the entirety of the first chronicle, none of us paid too close attention to the rules of magical tools. Retroactively, Winona is Ash's dedicated tool, making the weird affection he shows it make more sense.<br /> <br /> Unintentionally (though in some cases, more intentionally as things went on), if you want a good idea of the sort of emotional arc and trials Ash is to endure, there're some pretty strong parallels between them as the protagonist of that show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 04-26-2017, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T09:02:48-07:00","id":1083998,"title":"","content":"This might be a spoiler, but here's a thing about the Ripper: After this, it <i>never got mentioned again.</i> A part of me feels that's fair - after all, the Ripper was this terrifying murderbeast; why would rank apprentices be sent after it? - but another part of me is sad it was never given more depth. Then again, by that point, the game wasn't terribly far from dying, so it's not surprising.<br /> <br /> I did later go back and invest more time in the Ripper as a concept in one of the solo game spin-offs from this, retroactively adding more detail to it. I won't go into the <i>why</i> of it yet, since that'd give away spoilers, but Malthus didn't have his named disciples until much later on, except for the Ripper.<br /> <br /> Eventually, we ended up with the Third Disciple, Ripper of Essential Form; the Fifth Disciple, Wandering Dark Star for Whom the Void is Reserved; the Ninth Disciple, [Name Redacted]; and the Twelfth Disciple, Miwok, the Burdened Scribe of the Rite of Carrion. When we get more detail on Malthus, I'll do my own post on each of them.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Something else I want to add: Games finding their feet. A lot of an early game is finding who the characters are and what the tone of the game is. The more experience you get with this stuff, the less time it takes, but there really is a lot of time spent with both the players and the ST figuring out who the characters are. Early on in this, I was pulling a lot of stuff from The Phantom for Kismet, Indiana Jones for Midas, and I am pretty sure the reason [REDACTED] happened with Ash is because Biston and I were both watching Farscape and reading Transmetropolitan around this time.<br /> <br /> It's way easier to get a mental image of Ash if you picture Spider Jerusalem running around naked.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, games tend to find their feet faster because I do way more groundwork on them, but even so, there's a lot of feeling out, especially if you're a player, to get to know the characters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T09:10:05-07:00","id":1084001,"title":"","content":"Got in because of the title (hey, that book was great), remained because of the content. This has been a truly enjoyable read. I'll keep following for sure","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T13:04:56-07:00","id":1084113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1075297-ash-dies-at-the-end-an-actual-play?p=1084001#post1084001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got in because of the title (hey, that book was great), remained because of the content. This has been a truly enjoyable read. I'll keep following for sure</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope it continues to be. It's been a while since I've written anything of size or substance, so this is as much me cutting my teeth and getting back into practice.<br /> <br /> If you or anyone else is expecting references or parallels to <i>John Dies at the End</i>, you're probably going to be disappointed. I've not read the book or seen the movie, and I titled this what I did because it's a truism. This is a story, I feel, about the transformative powers of magic and of the wider supernatural world: how they can make someone, ruin them, break them together, and make them someone new. In an optimistic sense, it's a story about someone becoming who they really are. In another sense, it's about how magic can destroy a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T23:07:30-07:00","id":1086082,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Chapter 4: Ripper Man(?)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Part 4</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> By the time Kismet and Midas return to speak with Tartarus, he, Ash, and Orcus are already in a shouting match, exchanging incredulities, insults, and passionate attempts to get things back on track (respectively). Ash hasn\u2019t changed back into his clothes, apparently feeling this news was more important than his dignity. When the two mags approach, Tartarus storms off, pausing for a second to offer them a nod and a perfunctory \u201cgood job.\u201d Ash continues to solidify his position on everyone\u2019s shitlists by giving Tartarus a parting finger, which earns him what he\u2019s sure is a glare from Orcus.<br /> <br /> \u201cAsh, if you don\u2019t calm down, I will take away your \u2018happy powder,\u2019\u201d Orcus threatens, with more than a little strain. Ash huffs at him, but doesn\u2019t challenge the Councilor\u2014the man looks old enough to turn him into sand, and the last thing he wants is for his stash to suddenly be turned into drywall. \u201cI want to talk to you before you go,\u201d Orcus continues, then departs before Ash can think of some excuse to not do so.<br /> <br /> Midas clears his throat to try and get Ash\u2019s attention. Ash waves over his shoulder, bending over to rifle through the pile of clothes on the floor beside him.<br /> <br /> Kismet grimaces. \u201cCould you <i>please</i> put your pants back on?\u201d she asks.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing, stormtrooper,\u201d Ash grumbles, stopping his search for whatever to pull his pants from the pile and tug them back on. A second later he pulls what he was searching for out of his pocket: a packet of cigarettes.<br /> <br /> ~ ~ ~<br /> <br /> \u201cAccording to Tartarus, he put Malthus in the ground decades ago. Stabbed a spear through his heart,\u201d Ash says, lighting a cigarette with a burning thumb. \u201cA Tremere, pretty powerful, and with a hell of a cult of personality. From what I picked up on, Tartarus was taking care of some other people in green cloaks while we were following up on the Ripper.\u201d<br /> <br /> The cabal has taken a seat in a conference room with a small rectangular table and an unused wall-length whiteboard.<br /> <br /> Kismet frowns. \u201cThe sign says \u2018no smoking,\u2019\u201d she says. Ash blows a cloud of smoke into her face, which she doesn\u2019t react to.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnyway,\u201d Ash continues, \u201cthey were saying things the two of them really wished they hadn\u2019t around me. Got very upset when I suggested we could do something to help.\u201d He frowns. \u201cThere was plenty they weren\u2019t saying, but I picked up on some of it. Tartarus thinks Malthus is trying to build a\u2026 well\u2026\u201d Ash leans in, whispering. \u201cA <i>Ladder</i>.\u201d He shifts uncomfortably.<br /> <br /> A silence falls over the three of them. Ash\u2019s eyes dart expectantly between the two of them, looking for a reaction.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not our business,\u201d Midas finally declares, though he doesn\u2019t look committed to it. \u201cI know you might have reservations, Ash, but I\u2019ve picked at things I\u2019m not suited for, and-\u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cI agree,\u201d Ash interrupts, and Midas exhales. \u201cI don\u2019t know much, but\u2026 this is really far above what we\u2019re good for. And it has nothing to do with us,\u201d he insists.<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. Nothing to do with us,\u201d Kismet echoes, staring off into nothing.<br /> <br /> Ash falls back into his seat, spouting twin gouts of smoke from his nose. \u201cOh thank God, I was afraid one of us was going to be stupid about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a moment of awkward silence, all three of them knowing their business is concluded but that they have no common ground to make small-talk with. Finally, Midas speaks.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe should find a place to work,\u201d Midas blurts out. Ash gives a curt nod. They both look towards Kismet.<br /> <br /> Kismet sighs. \u201cFine, I\u2019ll see what I can\u2026 see,\u201d she offers, awkwardly.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eh4plfU1GCA\" target=\"_blank\">As Ash stands to go have his chat with Orcus, Kismet resumes off into space. She thinks of the man who claimed to be Malthus, unable to forget those empty eyes or the green glow in their depths. The resurrected master building some horrible bridge between heaven and earth. \u2018Come back to me,\u2019 she hears again in her head, and she can imagine the Tremere sitting on the edge of oblivion, a writhing pillar to his side at he stares into the absolute ends of everything. He\u2019d be wearing a thin-lipped smile on his corpse-skin face at their recent encounter, having found whatever it was he\u2019d been looking for in her.<br /> <br /> \u201cNothing to do with us,\u201d Kismet says again, as Midas watches her with concern<br /> <br /> &quot;Adelaide was asking about you,&quot; Midas says, and Kismet focuses on that, doing her best not to imagine what the Tremere's laugh would sound like.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> <br /> I would include Ash's chat with Orcus, but I remember little of it, and what I do remember is that overall it was just Orcus trying to convince Ash of the worthwhileness of Ash's own order. It provided some insight into the characters, but to read and play it was just several hours of Orcus going &quot;come on&quot; and Ash responding with canned iconoclasy--not fun to read or reconstruct from memory. What did come out of it was Ash actually trusting Orcus more, but there are other places to showcase that.<br /> <br /> What is on display here is Ash's contempt for his own cabal, a running element in this chronicle and beyond. At this juncture, he at least has some respect for Midas as someone who has accomplished things and has a visible moral compass, but Kismet... well, Kismet never had a chance. She was an outlet for his hatred of mage society, focusing on her affiliations as a Guardian--views put in his head by Goch, a man whose father and father's associates were affiliated with actual Nazis and were directly and indirectly responsible for the difficulties of Ash's formative years.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Chapter 2 is over with. I would've liked to have done it in fewer updates, but I've been putting these out as time is made available to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 05-01-2017, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T09:38:00-07:00","id":1086226,"title":"","content":"I am the Midas in this story.<br /> <br /> At the encouragement of Biston and against my better judgment, I decided to make an account and throw some of my perspective into this bubbling cauldron of weirdness. I think Biston prefaced that he\u2019s telling his version of the story with some retcons that were appropriate to Ash\u2019s continued solo adventures. I\u2019ll probably end up doing the same, but I don\u2019t think any of these changes are major. From what I\u2019ve seen of Biston\u2019s adjustments so far, his changes just smooth out minor wrinkles.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s give it a go.<br /> <br /> Biston\u2019s description of Midas in Chronicle I is accurate. Midas, real name David Snow, was a teacher who Awakened as an alchemist and joined the Mysterium under Adelaide\u2019s tutelage. He\u2019s my first Mage character and really my first attempt at a World of Darkness experience, period. Biston was also right about struggling to nail down themes and figuring out how to make this all work in a game with a cabal.<br /> <br /> Blood and Spiders seems like it had some red flags. I really enjoyed the adventure and still think fondly of it, even if I know better that wizarding usually doesn\u2019t work this way. Like Biston said, Midas was actually the first of the cabal to be created; Axelgear ran this as a solo game for me for a while before bringing in Biston and our other player. I think this explains some of the design choices made on that adventure. By this point, Midas had been adventuring enough that he had some reasonably established themes, and one of those themes was a cavalier Indiana Jones adventuring style. Most of his work in the Mysterium has been artifact-hunting, and by the time this game started, I think he\u2019d had at least two major adventures in that vein: uncovering an ancient alchemist\u2019s laboratory near the library of Alexandria and tracking down a similarly ancient monastery in Tibet. Both were great fun, globetrotting adventures, and gallivanting off to Central America to recover an artifact from a Mayan temple was right in line with this. Midas had taken on the Victorian-era explorer look for wizardly meetings because of these travels; dashing coat, sturdy boots, even a fancy cane that he enchanted to fight with if he had to.<br /> <br /> When they came out of it, though, Midas\u2019 spirit was really at odds with Ash\u2019s. All the fear and blood dusted off of Midas amid the joy of discovery, and he came out of the portal all smiles. Ash, though, was the one who ended up vomiting/crying/bleeding spiders, and I think part of the disconnect was that I as a player just forgot that part by the end. When Ash went off angrily, rightly traumatized by what had happened, it was too late to act more sober. Still, we tried to make it seem friendly enough that the three of them had a good reason to stick together, and the cabal tentatively took shape.<br /> <br /> We know in hindsight now that things don\u2019t usually go this way with wizards in general or the Mysterium in particular, but I found the adventure fun at the time and sure wasn\u2019t gonna retcon it away. I remember hoping for the best at the time. Ash caught on that Midas was good with making things, and Midas agreed to make some parts for his magic machine. Seemed like a sign things might be okay.<br /> <br /> Things weren\u2019t okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13338-inari","name":"Inari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13338_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T02:40:57-07:00","id":1091468,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Interlude IV: Dream Machine</span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> When Ash tells Pathos about his dreams and their vaguely-prophetic bend, she immediately takes interest. The look on her face is one he\u2019s seen before, on the faces of his former colleagues; men and women who\u2019ve found something to bite into, to pull apart and learn from.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo they guided you to the club?\u201d Pathos presses one night as they\u2019re leaving after shutdown.<br /> <br /> \u201cI like to think they brought me to you,\u201d Ash replies with unwitting earnestness, scratching at the red ring left on his forehead by his frizzy-haired wig. It\u2019s become easy to rely on her, even over just a few months, and even these strange moments of openness have been becoming comfortable to him for the first time in his life.<br /> <br /> Pathos smiles at it, and thankfully doesn\u2019t acknowledge it any further. Instead, she proposes something.<br /> <br /> And that is how Ash found himself strapped around his chest to a padded wooden chair. \u201cI didn\u2019t figure you for the type,\u201d he jokes.<br /> <br /> Pathos snorts. \u201cDon\u2019t you start,\u201d she says. \u201cI want to see how your brain works when under like this,\u201d she explains as she polishes Ash\u2019s temples and attaches two discs to the sides of his head. \u201cWitcher wouldn\u2019t break us into the hospital, so I\u2019m improvising. These things will monitor and record, and I\u2019ll be doing one of my own using a spell and myself as a relay.\u201d She ruffles his hair. \u201cTry not to go insane in the middle of it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ash frowns slightly, and swallows his instinct to ask \u2018who\u2019s Witcher?\u2019 He finds something else to talk about. \u201cWe could try to build an EEG machine,\u201d he says.<br /> <br /> Pathos quirks a brow at him.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat? We have friends. could get some to make materials, we could easily make the right tools, download or divine plans\u2026\u201d Ash trails off, now down a road he\u2019s never thought on before. \u201cHell, what couldn\u2019t the right spells build?\u201d he wonders. He stiffens for a moment. \u201cA bunch of college kids made a working nuke frame,\u201d he remembers.<br /> <br /> Pathos stares at him for a second. \u201cNow I\u2019m going to have trouble sleeping. Thanks, Ash,\u201d she remarks with a strained smile. \u201cNow stop talking. I\u2019m going to take a final check, turn this thing on, and then we\u2019ll have you use the powder.\u201d<br /> <br /> Pathos drops a small purple pouch of off-white powder on the endtable beside Ash\u2019s chair before turning to do a last-minute go-over and calibration on the two computers she\u2019s set up for the sake of this project. When she turns back around a minute later, the entire pouch is empty, and Ash is sporting a heavy dust on his upper lip.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, both of them can hear a pin drop. Pathos\u2019s eyes are wide, staring at Ash. The small grin on Ash\u2019s own face is beginning to fade.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou were only supposed to have a pinch,\u201d Pathos remarks.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh,\u201d Ash says, before the sensation of falling starts to overtake him. The last sight he has before the world fades is Pathos running to his side.<br /> <br /> ~ ~ ~<br /> <br /> The world fades away from him, but Ash keeps falling. The blackness around him twinkles with stars, a firmament littered with four-pointed diamonds, and that ripples and undulates and begins to give way. Colors bleed in, slowly at first, but eventually they roll past at immense speed, a rainbow that slowly blurs into white. It\u2019s blinding.<br /> <br /> Ash flexes his wings, and soars towards it. That light is in front of him. It\u2019s at the end of the tunnel, and as he approaches it he watches it shrink, shivering before his approach. He hears the whine of exposed electricity, and as he does so an immense pain fills his chest. Loneliness, longing, regret. The pain of sin, the weight of guilt. It intensifies the closer he comes to his goal, the nearer he gets to holding the sun in the palm of his hand, all while it retreats into something smaller and smaller.<br /> <br /> Tears stream down Ash\u2019s cheeks. The memory of it, of all these things, His hand grasps. He screams in emotional anguish, and that weight on his chest explodes. Shards of obsidian tear free from his heart, forming a mushroom cloud of jagged glass that is stained with his blood. The sun explodes outwards as he closes his fingers on it. He feels heat and pain as it blows him past, singing away his body hair, his wings melting away in the fury of it all. Once again he is tumbling.<br /> <br /> Ash looks to his chest, and the glass falls away to reveal a large phage. Even without eyes he can feel it looking at him. It leaps from his chest, and he watches it and the glass scatter as a crater before Olympus Mons. He tumbles through the volcano.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou deserve this,\u201d Ash hears himself tell himself before he crashes into the sky, into a sea of tass. Above him hangs a moon, and on it an oversized ziggurat. It bleeds shimmering rainbow liquid wastefully into space. Before he knows it, Ash is crawling towards that bloody bridge.<br /> <br /> With reverence, with longing, with desperation, Ash reaches towards that impossibility with stained hands. He stumbles, weeping. When he looks back up, he\u2019s in the jungle, at the foot of that temple. Beyond the treeline, he can feel them there\u2014friends, Seers, spiders. He wipes away his tears, and as he stands the residual tass dries across him in whorling, runic patterns.<br /> <br /> It still hurts. Ash\u2019s body hurts, his heart hurts. Somehow, that feels fine now. It feels right to feel this way. It feels necessary.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou deserve this,\u201d Ash repeats to himself as he begins to climb the ziggurat.<br /> <br /> The peak of the ziggurat stretches further than it looks, and as he climbs the worn stone gives way to golden brick, and from golden brick to seemless, perfect curves and angles. The sky looms closer with each step, and in it is a gaping, yawning hole of blackness that contrasts with the city-light stars hanging around it. There is mist, and somewhere out in it he feel ten sets of eyes boring into him, and can imagine the monoliths of reclining kings they belong to. He sees silhouettes at the peak, always shifting and changing: a woman with a bodybuilder\u2019s figure, an old man in a cloak, one that shifts between man and woman, and many more.<br /> <br /> Ash\u2019s jaw is set, his gaze is hard as steel. He finally mounts the step to the precipice, and finds himself stepping into a crater of blood. It reaches up to his ankles. A friendly hand claps onto each shoulder. To his left he sees a pale man in a suit, and when the man grins he has two rows of teeth. To his right is an androgynous youth. Both of them are looking at him with confidence and pride.<br /> The grip the two have on Ash tightens, and he relaxes in their hold. He trusts them. He is resigned to this; he is <i>dedicated</i> to this. Their fingers dig in like talons. They pull.<br /> <br /> As Ash is divided, there is light.<br /> <br /> ~ ~ ~<br /> <br /> Ash gasps for air as he comes to, shaking violently. Pathos\u2019s face fills everything. Her eyes are bloodshot and her face is covered in sweat.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh my God,\u201d Pathos breathes as Ash\u2019s eyes focus on her. \u201cAsh, do you remember me?\u201d<br /> <br /> She\u2019s checking for brain damage, Ash immediately intuits. How long had he been out? A small imago and he knows the time\u2014Kismet\u2019s daily body-cleansing ritual would have just hit him, removing whatever it was he\u2019d been dying from from his body.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2019m fine,\u201d Ash coughs out, pulling himself into a sitting position. He\u2019s on the floor. \u201cI\u2019m fine,\u201d he rasps, this time clearer. His heart is going a mile a minute.<br /> <br /> Pathos slumps with relief. \u201cYou were- I tried CPR, and there wasn\u2019t a heartbeat-\u201c<br /> <br /> Pathos babbles. Ash suddenly notices that his ribs hurt, and that he tastes what he think might be lip gloss. He lingers, trying to hold on to those dreams. Eventually he notices Pathos has stopped talking and is staring expectantly at him. He says the only thing he can think to right now.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey don\u2019t do the breathing thing anymore,\u201d Ash blurts out. Pathos stares at him for a long second. Laughter begins to bubble from her, and she socks him hard enough in the shoulder to leave a bruise. Probably the point.<br /> <br /> \u201cI haven\u2019t taken a class since highschool,\u201d Pathos says. \u201cYou asshole.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ash smiles weakly back at her, both settling into a relieved silence. After a minute, with the adrenaline dying down, Pathos looks at Ash. He meets her gaze, and for a second he sees something there which makes him freeze. A pang of something. Pity? Concern? Either way, he needs to say something quick.<br /> <br /> \u201cWould you mind helping me with something I\u2019m working on?\u201d Ash asks, rubbing his aching chest.<br /> <br /> Pathos looks at him, and from her smirk and incredulous look he can read her mind: \u2018Are you kidding me?\u2019 He can\u2019t tell if it\u2019s supposed to be an affirmation or not.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve got Marx onboard,\u201d Ash continues.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> I admit, the original playthrough of this scene didn't happen this way. The events inside the dream were less-ambiguous and less-prophetic, and while I can't remember them fully well I think they involved Ash wandering through a Tron-like astral space before yelling at Exarchs while handing out plasma pistols.to guys without eyes on a floating island. Overall, it served no purpose aside from being a thing to do.<br /> <br /> I changed that.<br /> <br /> Sorry this broke from a semi-consistent update schedule, been busy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 05-12-2017, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T22:08:11-07:00","id":1093537,"title":"","content":"So, I've not posted in here for a while. Guess I should fix that.<br /> <br /> First, let me just say: The Ash-Midas conflict was big. I'm not going into it, because it's not entirely my story to tell, but that caused a fuck-ton of grief. Now, we're all best friends, but for the longest time, there was a lot of misery.<br /> <br /> What I do want to draw attention to here is Pathos.<br /> <br /> Pathos's role in Ash's story evolved with time, and with Ash. She was initially introduced as a buddy for Ash to relate to; someone who shared his particular interest in trying to introduce people to magic as a possibility and gradually uplift them (back when what counted as Obvious and how Disbelief worked were still somewhat unclear to everyone involved).<br /> <br /> That didn't last, though. Ash grew both past that and exponentially more powerful (something that got explained in-setting). So Pathos's role changed and, to be honest, she was one of the very few things that I think I did right.<br /> <br /> On the surface, Pathos seems like a reasonably well-adjusted person, who compassionately tries to help Ash because she sees a good person inside him. Truth is, though, Pathos is anything but well-adjusted or good for Ash. Across the stories, she broke her legs multiple times with Paradox Backlash trying to equal Ash's feats of sorcery. When that failed, she encouraged his own explorations in the manner shown above, essentially feeding his habits. She excused his bad behaviour, fed his ego, and essentially acted as his confessor; forgiving him the actions that pushed away everyone else. He sought her out whenever his life went to shit so that she'd dress his wounds (sometimes literally), assure him that it was all worth it, and promise that, no, really, he's still a good person.<br /> <br /> Pathos became a massive enabler, whose own life suffered for having Ash in it. She was the archetypal power-worshiping thearch, who misunderstood good intentions for good thinking.<br /> <br /> By the end, Ash couldn't have done what he did without her, and that should not be seen as a compliment.<br /> <br /> (I feel weird saying this as the ST, but this is me summarizing my conversations with Biston on the subject.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T01:59:31-07:00","id":1094048,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Chapter 3: The Lakehouse</b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> It\u2019s a long ride to south Oregon. Midas is in the driver\u2019s seat of an old blue truck. Kismet\u2019s on the passenger\u2019s seat, giving directions. Ash rides in the bed, wearing that ill-fitting suit again and clashing with the looser attire of his fellows. They find themselves going off-road, traveling through bumpy forests paths and managing to find partly-overgrown dirt roads that no longer connect to anything. Eventually, Kismet calls for them to stop in a place she says she saw in one of her divining visions. They pile out, surrounded by trees on all sides.<br /> <br /> Midas and Ash had asked Kismet to find them a place where they could work without issue, and had been following her castings since. She\u2019d consulted with Adelaide on her visions, and the mentor decided that it was as good a time as any for her to finally initiate into her legacy. This was why, when she produced an old-fashioned wineskin, nobody expressed any surprise.<br /> <br /> Kismet takes a swig from the wineskin, and offers some to Ash and Midas. Midas politely turns it down. Ash, on the other hand, regards it for a long moment. He and Kismet have been trying to mend their fences since he\u2019d terrorized her at her apartment\u2014some illusions he\u2019d produced with Prime and Forces when she\u2019d altered his blood-cleansing to make it impossible to get high. Not wanting to be rude, and as a gesture of solidarity, Ash takes the wineskin and drinks deep from it. After he does, Kismet tosses it back into the truck.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis way,\u201d Kismet says, guiding them.<br /> <br /> They trek through the woodland. As they move, they pick up speed, unsure steps to a power walk to an eventual run. Their breath comes more shallow, and it begins to seep in Ash: the water was drugged. For some reason that makes him want to giggle. Above him the moon leaves trails when he sees it through the treetops. Ahead, Kismet laughs into the night as she leads them in running through the forest, their hike graduating into a frenzied tear.<br /> <br /> Behind them, Midas pants as he tries to keep pace with his addled companions.<br /> <br /> They finally break the treeline, and emerge before a lake. Mist drifts in the night air, and the moon shines on the water. An island sits in the middle of the lake. Kismet runs to dive into the water, heading for it. When she leaps, she leaps farther than she should\u2019ve even been able to. She looks over her shoulder as she sails through the air, and sees Ash miming throwing something. In a moment, Midas is abruptly pulled from the shore and sent tumbling through the air. A second later Ash follows after.<br /> <br /> Ash skips the three of them across the lake, punting each of them with his command over gravity and motion before they hit the water. They land on the island, rolling across the ground. Ash and Kismet laugh at the moon, shining brightly through the mist. Midas dusts himself off and checks his jacket for tears.<br /> <br /> As Midas rises, he notices a mansion made of wood. At first glance it looks abandoned; the lights are off, the door is hanging open, and the place looks in need of repair. A quick spell later confirms it, and also that the roof probably leaks. Further examination of his surroundings reveals the half-fallen remains of a dock\u2014likely how the former tenants got to and from the place.<br /> <br /> As Kismet and Ash tears across the island, hollering and laughing, Midas notices something else. He walks through the mist for a clearer look, and confirms it. Five markets. Five spots where the grass looks off.<br /> <br /> Ash has his eyes closed as he twirls, delighting in the sensation. It\u2019s like he\u2019s flying\u2014and he\u2019d know, being capable of it. Everything feels so far away here, on this isolated little island. Outside is Goch and his Nazi records; outside is Tartarus\u2019s scowl and Orcus\u2019s disappointed eyes; outside are the memories of his parents; outside are spiders and Seers and more eyes. And he loves Midas and Kismet and Pathos. How could he ever have hated any of this? How could he have ever hated at all with all this before him and in his hands?<br /> <br /> Ash is clenching his jaw and eyes so tight it hurts (in a good way) when Midas clamps a hand on his shoulder. He opens his eyes and smiles at the Moros, and is about to go in for a hug when Midas speaks.<br /> <br /> \u201cPeople died here,\u201d Midas says, concern writ on his face. Ash feels his mood falter, and is about to try and come up with a reasonable explanation when Midas continues: \u201cFive graves. Their shades\u2014they\u2019re terrified. Something happned here,\u201d he says, grasping Ash tightly by the shoulders.<br /> <br /> Ash blinks at Midas, dumbstruck. He looks back up at the moon, watching it tail through his vision. He glances to see Kismet, bounding across the grounds towards an old well. Something is happening here with him and with her, something that has nothing and everything to do with whatever it is they\u2019d taken. For a moment, Ash thinks of letting it go. But Ash considers himself rational, and Ash is familiar enough with how decision-making can be affected by substances (hell, it\u2019s part of the reason he uses them).<br /> <br /> Ash clenches his eyes and teeth again, dipping down, imagining his mind and his thoughts and everything that could change them, and walls them off. When he opens his eyes, a semblance of clarity has returned to them. He still feels lightness in his chest and sees the way the drab colors of the night still manage to pop out at them, but it doesn\u2019t reach his head.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m okay,\u201d Ash tells Midas, who nods and lets him go. \u201cWe should tell Kismet,\u201d he declares, and turns to where he last saw her.<br /> <br /> Kismet is staring up at the moon. As Ash and Midas approach, a noticeable beam cuts through the thickening mist, falling upon the old well. She stares for a long time, and then beelines for it. She dives for it, aiming to plunge into it, and suddenly finds herself suspended in midair. She looks over her shoulder, and sees Ash with his arm outstretched, holding her in place.<br /> <br /> \u201cLet me go,\u201d Kismet commands. He doesn\u2019t. \u201cLet me go!\u201d she yells, writhing in the grip of his telekinesis. \u201cLet me go! Let me go!\u201d she continues to yell, tone becoming more frantic.<br /> <br /> Ash tries to talk over it. \u201cYou\u2019re about to jump into a well!\u201d he says. \u201cPeople died here, Kismet!\u201d he says, trying to blink away how that shaft of light seems to be growing brighter in his chemically-altered vision.<br /> <br /> \u201cLet me go!\u201d Kismet screams.<br /> <br /> \u201cSomething is playing on us!\u201d Ash yells back, determined to keep her restrained until she comes to her sense. There is another force here, and he\u2019s not letting any member of his team jump into a well in a drug-addled haze until they know what\u2019s gone on. Though he\u2019d probably not be inclined to let them jump into a well under most other circumstances, either.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s down there!\u201d Kismet screeches. \u201cI\u2019m down there! Let me go!\u201d<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eh7bneLa2ek\" target=\"_blank\">Kismet\u2019s cryptic screaming only reinforces Ash\u2019s resolve.<br /> <br /> Midas stance behind Ash, and he looks between the other two members of his cabal. He\u2019s concerned and uncertain what\u2019s going on, or what they should do about anything, Whether he should be helping Ash or helping Kismet.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can fix us?\u201d Ash asks Midas.<br /> <br /> Midas stares at Ash and meets the Obrimos\u2019s steely-if-a-bit-dilated gaze. He slowly nods.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo it,\u201d Ash orders.<br /> <br /> Midas stares at Ash for a long moment, and then he sees Kismet staring at the two of them in horror. She knows he\u2019s considering doing it. After a long moment of consideration, he holds out a hand towards Kismet, his palm open.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d Kismet breathes. \u201cNo!\u201d she screams.<br /> <br /> Midas closes his fist. Instantly, the euphoria drains away from Ash and Kismet, leaving them sober once again. The light on the well fades away.<br /> <br /> Kismet goes limp in Ash\u2019s telekinetic hold, and he drops her onto the grass. She crawls to the well and curls into the fetal position next to it. The other two can hear her crying. Between sobs, they catch words: \u201cShe\u2019s gone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDeal with her,\u201d Ash tells Midas. It hangs unspoken, but obvious: \u201cShe wouldn\u2019t want a thing to do with me.\u201d Midas nods, and looks ready to say something, but it falls dead in his mouth as he turns to check on Kismet.<br /> <br /> With his shoulders squared, Ash stalks off to the other side of the grounds, scowling. Of course it went this way. Of course things turned sour. He\u2019s made the right choice anyway, even if it\u2019s cost him any rapport he might\u2019ve been able to build with Kismet. He has the sudden urge to curse at the moon, but he bites it back. Later, he\u2019d learn that Kismet had been chasing her other half, something to do with the Legacy she\u2019d been chasing. What follows will be insistence he made the right choice based on what he knew, and an intense bitterness at Kismet and her mentor for not saying so.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> I remember none of us being happy with how this scene played out. Kismet didn't get to inititate into her Legacy, Ash ended up being the bad guy again, and Midas was party to both. Kismet was chasing the 'other half of her soul.' The Legacy she was pursuing is the Sodality of Tor (in case you didn't read/forgot from the character list), and I don't remember or know enough to really remark further on her journey or what was going on there.<br /> <br /> The bit mentioned at the beginning about Ash terrorizing Kismet at her apartment was something that we played out. Ash was incredibly upset at being denied his fixes when Kismet made it impossible for him to get drunk or high, and concocted some illusory thing where he made her think she was being haunted by demons and that Ash had committed suicide. It ended with her lifting the restriction and both of them bonding while being hotboxed from the massive pile of weed Ash had burned to create smoke.<br /> <br /> The lake they found was either inspired by Cauldron Lake from <i>Alan Wake</i> or the real-life <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crater_Lake\" target=\"_blank\">Crater Lake.</a> The former was inspired by the latter anyway, so it hardly matters. Without Axel weighing in, I'd suspect the latter just because he tends to do his research.<br /> <br /> I'm looking forward to writing the next installment. It's where things, in my mind, really begin with Ash. It's such a damn shame it's going to start with such a silly thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 05-18-2017, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T01:53:53-07:00","id":1095064,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Chapter 4: Reaching Too Far<br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Part 1</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, that one.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEasy. Ursa Major.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright, hardmode: no magic. That one.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ash winces, staring up at the night sky. He and Marx are on their backs on the catwalk surrounding the dome of the mountaintop Peakstone Observatory. It\u2019s unstaffed tonight, making it perfect for their designs. Ash is wearing that same ill-fitting suit and Marx is in casual clothes, though wearing her metal gauntlets.<br /> <br /> \u201cUh\u2026 the Big Dipper?\u201d Ash says, glancing over at Marx.<br /> <br /> \u201cPleiades,\u201d Marx says, grinning at him. \u201cFor a guy who studies orbits \u2018n shit you don\u2019t know much about stars.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u201cWhen we studied stars it was more about how they moved and what they were made of,\u201d Ash mumbles. \u201cMy major wasn\u2019t astrophysics.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds like an excuse,\u201d Marx taunts.<br /> <br /> Ash grumbles. \u201cYou have any more of that stuff?\u201d he asks, changing the subject.<br /> <br /> \u201cNah. Only brought two doses. Figured I should be thinking straight for this,\u201d Marx explains.<br /> <br /> The sound of footsteps and creaking wheels approach from a distance, and Ash sits up to peer through the catwalk bars. Pathos is struggling up the road to the observatory, two gas canisters on a small dolly she\u2019s pulling behind her.<br /> <br /> Ash bangs excitedly on the metal frame. \u201cAnd the supplies are here!\u201d he declares. He slips under the bars, and floats down to the ground. By the time Marx has run down the observatory stairs, Pathos has reached them.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou assholes could\u2019ve opened a portal, you know,\u201d Pathos grouses at Marx and Ash, wiping sweat from her dark forehead. Marx opens her mouth to say something, then closes it and looks sheepish.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, don\u2019t glower at me, I don\u2019t know Space,\u201d Ash defends, taking the dolly\u2019s handle from Pathos. The three of them head into the building. \u201cHey, guys, a latina, a white, and a black enter an observatory\u2026\u201d he starts off and lets it hang, looking over his shoulder.<br /> <br /> Pathos is staring at Ash neutrally. \u201c\u2019A black?\u2019\u201d she repeats.<br /> <br /> Ash winces, and hisses a breath through his teeth. \u201cOoh,\u201d he sighs. \u201cSorry- wait, it\u2019s supposed to sound racist,\u201d he says.<br /> <br /> Pathos quirks a brow at Ash, amused at his ability to jam both feet into his mouth.<br /> <br /> \u201cNevermind, I\u2019ll just call up when I\u2019m done digging myself this hole,\u201d Ash mutters through the hand he\u2019s covered his face with.<br /> <br /> Marx claps Ash on the shoulder, her gauntlet undoubtably leaving a bruise. She chuckles. \u201cJust puttin\u2019 the best foot forward tonight, ain\u2019tcha?\u201d she asks.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey!\u201d Ash points defensively at Marx. \u201cAfter tonight, it\u2019ll be like we\u2019ve all run a mile anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> ~ ~ ~<br /> <br /> Marx had pulled a few accessories through a portal. Ash is leaning against a folding table while Marx is busy pinning photos from the Voyager II mission to a postboard. Pathos is currently working to make an elaborate harness of straps and buckles when she notices the hard look Ash is leveling at nothing.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you okay?\u201d Pathos asks Ash.<br /> <br /> It takes a second before Ash realizes he\u2019s been addressed. \u201cOh, oh, yeah,\u201d he says dismissively, not looking towards her.<br /> <br /> Pathos waits for a moment, then says \u201cyou\u2019re thinking about something.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ash waves his hand dismissively. \u201cNo, it\u2019s just\u2026 d\u00e9j\u00e0 vu. For some reason this is reminding me of a dream I\u2019ve been having. It\u2019s a lake, and the water start to move. Like if Nessie was surfacing but in a bunch of places. And I think \u2018Daoine.\u2019 Looked it up, means \u2018Good Folk,\u2019 Irish folklore, some etymologic roots. It\u2019s weird. And it\u2019s weirder I\u2019m feeling like this was in it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Pathos watches Ash for a long moment. \u201cAsh, maybe it\u2019s a coincidence, but there\u2019s a gulmoth in Lake Michigan called that. It\u2019s been haunting Chicago for centuries.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ash stiffens. \u201cChicago hasn\u2019t been around for centuries,\u201d he says. \u201cHow do you know that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA friend of my mentor lives there. He talked about it the last time he visited,\u201d Pathos explains.<br /> <br /> \u201cMidas is from Chicago. More goddamn signs,\u201d Ash mutters. \u201cI almost hate sleeping now.\u201d<br /> <br /> An uncomfortable silence hangs over them both, until finally Pathos breaks it. \u201cSo why did we need to do this here?\u201d she asks, awkwardly.<br /> <br /> Ash shrugs. \u201cMarx says it\u2019s the sympathies. I\u2019m still trying to think of an explanation on how none of us are going back in time whenever she opens one of those portals of hers.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marx walks back over and also leans against the table. \u201cAnd maybe when you stop thinking about it, you\u2019ll figure it out,\u201d she says with an edge of smug. \u201cAnyway, which one do we go with?\u201d she asks, gesturing towards the photo collage.<br /> <br /> All three of their eyes roam over the images. Ash\u2019s linger on one in particular. \u201cThat one,\u201d he says, pointing.<br /> <br /> ~ ~ ~<br /> <br /> Pathos is rigging the harness to the gas tanks while Ash switches on the fog machine. He\u2019s not sure why Marx needs the fog machine, but she\u2019s the Master, even if it feels stupid and wasteful to him.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow long have you been waiting to do this?\u201d Pathos asks.<br /> <br /> \u201cDidn\u2019t think of it until two months ago. I\u2019ve only been at this for six months, so I haven\u2019t had that much time yet,\u201d Ash says, not looking up.<br /> <br /> Pathos snorts. \u201cCome on, Ash. I\u2019m an Obrimos too. I\u2019ve seen your Nimbus.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ash shrugs. \u201cI\u2019ve only been at this six months. I told you that already, remember? When you tried to levitate that guy during your show and broke your leg, and I visited at the hospital?\u201d He pauses. \u201cOh shit, I forgot all about that, sorry we had you haul the tanks up here!\u201d<br /> <br /> Pathos waves it off, though she does unconsciously rub the temporary brace she\u2019s wearing beneath her pants. \u201cI thought you were patronizing me,\u201d she says, sounding smaller.<br /> <br /> Ash doesn\u2019t pick up on it. \u201cWouldn\u2019t dream of it,\u201d he says. Satisfied that the fog machine is now spewing fog, he rises and makes his way to Pathos and her apparatus. \u201cAre we set?\u201d he asks.<br /> <br /> Pathos stares at Ash for a long moment. \u201cY-yeah,\u201d she says. \u201cJust tighten here, these around the shoulders, buckle here-\u201c she lists off the system she\u2019s set up.<br /> <br /> Ash claps his hands together and rubs them like a madman about to throw some sinister switch. He skitters over to his breathing apparatus, shrugging into it and following Pathos\u2019s instructions. The breathing mask goes over his face, earbuds are placed in his ears, and for the finishing touch he dons his shades.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fhif fill fe th fiffest fmn leaf wev taken in ur hifory--Fleefr and Awakened!&quot; Ash muffles through the mask.<br /> <br /> &quot;Suffering succotash...&quot; Pathos murmurs underneath her breath, unable to help a smirk as she walks with Ash towards the stairs and directs him to go first. Rising up through the artificial fog like some great, holy diver, he approaches Marx on the interior catwalk.<br /> <br /> Marx has constructed a diagram against the closed doors of the observatory dome, something Ash recognizes as a diagram of the system and a rough map of the Voyager II\u2019s path. The destination moon is at the center of it, with two long swooshes to the side like a sideways eye or portal yet to be wrenched open.<br /> <br /> Ash can feel the magic moving in the room. Flowing... Drifting towards that central mark. The mist, against the pull of gravity, rises towards the mark on the wall.<br /> <br /> &quot;Alright... Think I've got a hang on it...&quot; Marx says quietly as she draws her fingers through the rote mudra positions over and over. The spell is not an easy one; it takes a great degree of effort and concentration and it doesn't take much to realize that such a thing is unusual for the practiced council elder.<br /> <br /> Ash takes a second to appreciate how odd it is that a woman that can\u2019t be out of her mid-twenties can be called an elder.<br /> <br /> &quot;I... I'm having some trouble here...\u201d Marx says, her voice strained. \u201cIt feels like...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Mfff fhrt?&quot; Ash asks.<br /> <br /> Ash can feel it before Marx answers. So can Pathos, so strongly that she grips her injured leg reflexively. There is an overwhelming sensation of it as Marx's aura becomes briefly tangible; the distant tolling of steel hammers on the anvils of the Proletariat before becoming the rumble and roar of Soviet rockets in flight. Ash can feel the pack he wears getting heavier, a headache starting to come up on him; pressure at the base of his neck. The feeling of insects crawling under his skin. He knows precisely what it is before Marx even says it: &quot;Paradox!&quot;<br /> <br /> Ash rips the mask off his face, instantly shouting. &quot;But nobody's he-&quot; His eyes go wide, and a look between excitement and horror creeps onto his face. Dreams of distant, seated figures peering down at him through the mists, silent, judging. Observing. &quot;They're here,&quot; he utters breathlessly. &quot;They're here!&quot; he cries. &quot;They know!&quot;<br /> <br /> With manic energy, Ash dashes across the floor, towards Marx and the portal. His steps clomp as the pack weighs him down to a heavy waddle. &quot;Marx! The Exarchs!&quot; he screams, glancing between her and the portal. &quot;Keep going or shut it down! It's in your hands now!&quot;<br /> <br /> Marx already seems to be on top of the issue when Ash starts to panic. Reaching out, she holds her hands up to the portal, draws the mudra backwards and... it does absolutely nothing. A splintering crack begins to form up the middle of the wall, through which the shrieks and cries of a million tortured souls can be heard. They form the wail of a tempestuous storm. Repeating the gesture again and again, Marx can only watch as the room begins to shudder, the railings begin to shake. Reflexively, she dives for something to grab onto, looking back to Ash and reaching out towards him.<br /> <br /> Ash dives for Marx. He feels a sudden chill race over him. Everything goes dark.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> So first thing to mention: Marx and Pathos are latina and black, respectively. I don't believe I've mentioned that yet in anything related to them, so it'll probably get edited in somewhere. It slipped my mind to do so thusfar because, while it is important, it never really came up.<br /> <br /> Commentary errata for whether or not Space could scry or open portals to other planets exists for 1E. I don't believe any commentary on it presently exists for 2E. We weren't aware of the errata at the first time we played, and it's something I'm surprised isn't covered in the core. Simply put, if I was given the power to open doors to places via photograph, my first inclination would be to try and go to Mars, and it's weird how there's not documentation of a bunch of mages trying to post-1969. If it did or didn't work then there'd be a bunch of theories in the mage community on Earth and magic and sympathies and so on.<br /> <br /> On a positive note: I actually have logs for (most) of this chapter. If you noticed a change in style in this post, it's because I stopped needing to write material as I remembered it and could instead begin doctoring, editing, and adapting those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T06:58:12-07:00","id":1095889,"title":"","content":"There's a reason Biston has the logs for this part of the game: It's the point when it starts going LA LA LA~ off into crazy town. The crazy train has crested the hill, the brakes are gone, and the municipality of crazy town lies at the bottom.<br /> <br /> It's honestly also where the game got a lot harder for me. Don't get me wrong, I loved the places Ash's stuff went, but keeping up with the rising tempo got difficult fast. Another lesson I'd give to any new ST - and one it took me too damn long to learn - is that not everything needs to top what came before. Ideally, it doesn't. You just can't sustain it. Yes, games should have rising arcs, with the scope and scale of the characters' deeds rising with time, but it shouldn't be a race to the top of the mountain.<br /> <br /> This game went its own unique way. In future, though, I ended up feeling a need to be a bit more cautious with XP hand-outs and the whole sense of grand destiny. It's fun sometimes, to be sure, but you don't want everything to feel like a rocket ride to the finish line.<br /> <br /> Also, because Biston neglected to add music. I figure it's my duty to do so. At first, I thought Gamma Ray's Into the Black Hole might work, but then <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AJsrcbVGsa4\" target=\"_blank\">I remembered this existed.</a><br /> <br /> Edit: And ignore the actual video. Good grief, please ignore it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","user":"Axelgear","date":". 05-23-2017, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T07:42:19-07:00","id":1095906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1075297-ash-dies-at-the-end-an-actual-play?p=1095889#post1095889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason Biston has the logs for this part of the game: It's the point when it starts going LA LA LA~ off into crazy town. The crazy train has crested the hill, the brakes are gone, and the municipality of crazy town lies at the bottom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to say that two games budded off from here. One was balls-to-the-wall, batshit insane lunacy that was dedicated to stretching the system to its limits and taking things to their highly-illogical conclusions. The other one was a serious and dramatic story about what magic does to a person and the amorality of ambition in the context of the Supernal.<br /> <br /> We'll be covering the second game first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This game went its own unique way. In future, though, I ended up feeling a need to be a bit more cautious with XP hand-outs and the whole sense of grand destiny. It's fun sometimes, to be sure, but you don't want everything to feel like a rocket ride to the finish line. </div> </div> </div>To expand on this, we were playing in 1E at this point and Axel was providing us lots of XP for what we were doing, both interludes and otherwise. 1E costs grew exponentially and we were running this over a text program, making it so that a single scene could take multiple sessions, depending on its density. This meant we were all increasing in power dramatically fast. Ultimately this was explained (and not in any &quot;Chosen One&quot; sort of sense), and all I'm inclined to say at this point is that it was a surprisingly appropriate coincidence that the 1E to 2E transition had dragons go from being an image in the calling of humanity to magic, to demonized figures in Tremere myth.<br /> <br /> It's hard to remember exact numbers, but at this stage in the game Ash had at least Gnosis 4, Forces 4, Mind 2 or 3, and Prime 2 or 3, to give you all an idea of the level of skill the cabal was throwing about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, because Biston neglected to add music. I figure it's my duty to do so. At first, I thought Gamma Ray's Into the Black Hole might work, but then <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AJsrcbVGsa4\" target=\"_blank\">I remembered this existed.</a> </div> </div> </div>Holy shit, official theme to the Ashgame, right here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T04:04:07-07:00","id":1097740,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Chapter 4: Reaching Too Far</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Part 2</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Ash...&quot; A soft voice whispers in his ear.<br /> <br /> &quot;Aaaash...&quot; A gentle shake and nudge at the arm.<br /> <br /> &quot;Time to get up, sleepyhead.&quot; It is a warm, rather familiar voice, as Ash wakes up in what appears to be a hospital room. Pathos is leaning over him, her hands on his shoulders to rouse him from sleep. Her smile is gentle and kind. &quot;Come on. Eyes open, soldier. It's time for breakfast.&quot;<br /> <br /> Confused and frightened, Ash immediately bolts up and tears at his blankets, desperately trying to untangle them from his legs. &quot;Where are they?! Where is she?!&quot; He shrieks, eyes bulging out of his skull. Already his face is beginning to turn red as the combination, of terror, concern, and red fury stir around in his head and heart.<br /> <br /> Pathos jumps back, almost tripping to the floor with her leg on her brace. Scrambling to get up, Ash finds his head pounding, his vision almost a blur. His blood pounds in his ears for a moment before that animal part of him forces him to look around. The smell of disinfectants, the clattering of his metal bed. He gets a view of the room he is in: Small. White walls. A sink. A mirror. A door with a small window. Tube lighting lined the ceiling.<br /> <br /> Pathos stands nearby, dressed in loose white. A nametag on her shirt reads &quot;Patricia Ravenston&quot; but, below it, the word Pathos is scrawled in pen. &quot;Woah, woah, woah!&quot; She calls out to Ash. &quot;Eeeeasy... Easy... Calm down, Avery. Where's who?&quot;<br /> <br /> Ash freezes as his surroundings sink in. He knows them too damn well. Those visits in the twilight of his teenage years, the crying and the screaming and the catatonia. All loss and tragedy and fear, and the utter fragility of the mind. The color drains from his face. The tendency for certain disorders to run in the family, voices which had haunted him for his entire life- voices he wasn't hearing. Shaking, he stares at Patricia- Pathos- whatever, desperate to ground himself in the world he knows.<br /> <br /> &quot;They can get in your head- in your dreams.&quot; It spills from Ash\u2019s lips. &quot;Lie to you, trick you. Dogs and masters, tools and leashes for rungs down a ladder. Paradox.&quot; His breathing increases, the anger and panic returning. &quot;Lie to me. Go on. See if you can do it,&quot; he challenges.<br /> <br /> Pathos gives a slow nod, watching Ash as he perches on his bed and rants at her. Edging away, she moves towards his sink and picks up a small orange, white-capped container there. She moves towards him slowly. &quot;Don't worry, Avery, this room is safe. Protected against the Exarchs. We made sure together, remember?&quot; she assures him, carefully pouring a pill into her hand. Ash's keen eyes can read the label; 5mg of clopenthixol. &quot;We can go over the wards again, if you like? You just have to take your pill and come have some breakfast. I can maybe even ask Dr. O. if he's got some more files for you to look at for your big project.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u201cNo thanks,&quot; Ash replies, coolly. &quot;I'm leaving. Thanks for the dream trip but I've books. I saw Buffy the Vampire Slayer. I'm good.&quot; Ash swings his legs over the side of the bed. He pulls himself to his feet and makes towards the exit. &quot;You had me for just a second.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Avery, if you don't take your medication on time, the visions are only going to get worse.&quot; Pathos warns him, following behind. &quot;Now, you can have breakfast with it, but you're going to have to take it very soon after or you'll mess up the schedule. I don't think anyone wants another 'incident' like you had a few weeks ago.&quot; There was a pause after a few steps. &quot;Avery, don't make me get your mother!&quot;<br /> <br /> Ash stops mid-step, the death-fury in his eyes thankfully hidden from the supposed nurse. His foot hangs in the air. &quot;Actually, I'd like to go see Dr. O before breakfast, I had a wonderful idea I'd like to share with him. Oh, and my mother. Just can't wait, you know.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pathos gives a sigh, pinching her brow unhappily. &quot;Alright... If I take you to see Doctor O., will you promise to take your medicine? He won't want to talk with you unless you take your medication.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You should know by now, Path- Patricia!&quot; Ash declaires, pointing a finger skyward. &quot;I don't promise anything! I bargain! I have given you my terms!&quot; If the bastards want a show, he\u2019ll give them one.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh dear...&quot; Pathos gave a sigh. &quot;Alright, very well...&quot; She sighs and lead Ash through the hallways, towards an office. As they walk, Ash can't help but notice the walls start to repeat, the scenery purely on a loop, until they came to an office labeled simply &quot;Dr. O.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pathos knocks on the office door. A voice answers: &quot;Come in!&quot; And the office opens to reveal a man sitting at a desk, scrivening at reports; a man in a doctor's coat and wearing a formal shirt and a stethoscope and... and... and he only has half a head. It rises to the bridge of his nose and stops abruptly there. Otherwise, it;s Orcus to a T. Of course, Ash hadn\u2019t seen any more of Orcus than that; the man never lifted his hood above the edge of his nose.<br /> <br /> Ash bursts into desperate laughter, his upper lip curled up so much he almost looks like a donkey baying. &quot;Knew it!&quot; he declares, pointing both fingers at- -should he think of it as Us or Orc?--the facsimile. He chuckles and immediately turns on his heel. &quot;I'm out of here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Except the door is no longer there. When Ash turns back around, the Pathos doppelganger has vanished.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, I figured, if you're not going to make an effort, I might as well not bother either...&quot; The doctor at the table remarked rather languidly. He doesn\u2019t seem to have minded Ash\u2019s derision; in fact, he\u2019s smiling good-naturedly, showing off two sets of teeth. &quot;I mean, really, I might as well be honest; you'd have suffered horrendously either way but you'd probably have personally suffered less if you'd just gone along with it. Honestly, would it have been so bad?&quot; The 'doctor' muses, scribbling slowly at the table.<br /> <br /> When Ash looks back in the other direction, the windows to the office were gone, too.<br /> <br /> &quot;But I suppose I can have my fun with the others, instead,\u201d Not-Orcus declares, pausing briefly to tilt what little head he has up. Ash gets the impression the thing is trying to give him a pointed look.<br /> <br /> Ash plops down into the chair on the opposite side of Orcass's desk. He grabs the facsimile's appointment flapper, kicks his feet up on the table, and begins to go through it, petulantly tearing pages out as he goes. They\u2019re all blank. He checks the business cards. Also blank. Even the paper the monster is writing on is blank.<br /> <br /> &quot;You want something from me,&quot; Ash declares plainly. &quot;Or you would've killed me or put me in a world where the air is acid and the floor is razorblades, assuming you can do that.&quot; Ash takes one of the blank cards and tosses it above Orcass's head, trying to drift it inside the empty top half of his skull. &quot;Or maybe you're just a sadistic bastard. But that was a remark either meant to draw me in or torment me with supposed powerlessness, so let's rap. Are you my Good Folk-\u201c the walls shiver for a moment at Daoine\u2019s other name \u201c-or just some other horrible chthonic thing who wants to make me suffer.&quot; He peers over one card. &quot;Or are you someone else?&quot;<br /> <br /> The pen the outsider was using is gone, now. So are the papers Ash has tossed on the floor.<br /> <br /> &quot;Not. Worth. The time.&quot; The outsider says simply before going through the motions of stopping and setting down an invisible pen. &quot;I will say this, though: your plan was interesting. Imaginative. Unique. You're not the first to try it but... Well, you can see why the records of the attempt don't tend to exactly last long.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait,&quot; Ash blurts, a bit frustrated with having to give even a tiny bit of acknowledgement that he is out of his depth. &quot;You've said the words you know will get a rise out of me. I'm humbled.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ash presses his fingers hard against his closed eyes. He envisions an imago, aura sight and an aegis. The spells don\u2019t come\u2014not like they\u2019re supposed to. Instead he feels a warm tingle cross around his body, and it pools in his right hand. It runs back and forth along his forearm, a moving tingle like his arm is falling asleep. When he opens his eyes again, he sees the outsider ringed by a yawning blackness.<br /> <br /> &quot;So you've had to stop transplanetary travel before? I'm not the first?&quot; Ash asks. He appears wounded at the idea, like mommy had just told little Billy that he isn't special.<br /> <br /> &quot;Had to stop?&quot; The desk-bound facsimile echoes, then chuckles. &quot;You poor sap; the Void is not the province of Mages! We don't need to try and 'stop' you. You laid out the welcome mat for us! We were happy to oblige.&quot; The outsider\u2019s smile turns dark. &quot;Ever since you monkeys got telescopes, you've tried to reach the Celestial Spheres, and you always forget the medium through which you must tunnel to reach them.&quot;<br /> <br /> That strikes a chord. &quot;The same medium we tunnel through to get anywhere else,&quot; he replies, refusing to compromise his understanding of space-time. The tingle in his arm resonates in time with that frustration. &quot;Unless you want to tell me that everything from the Abyss is floating in outer space like something from H.P. Lovecraft's nightmares.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Wouldn't that be fun?&quot; The man at the desk laughs. &quot;Of course, perhaps the creatures of the Abyss exist everywhere, simultaneously, between the spaces; the space between your every atom swarming with Gulmoths.&quot; His smile grows wider, and he starts to tap his fingers together. &quot;Or perhaps space itself is the Abyss. After all, people do claim that the moon landings were faked. Maybe they really were; faked by Mages. Or perhaps I'm an alien and this isn't about the Abyss at all!&quot; He says, then leans forward on the desk. &quot;Or perhaps your rambunctious efforts really could bring about a blow to those seated on the thrones in Heaven, and I am truly an Exarch, reaching down to swat you like the fly you are...&quot;<br /> <br /> As the man talks, Ash focuses on that nervous, shifting energy running up his arm. There\u2019s a tugging at it, as if he\u2019s hooked or has hooked something, and its straining across the distance between them. He tries to grasp it, tries to think of an imago that might do something, and realizes: the pull is coming from the man across from him, or through him, past whatever intrusion it is he represents.<br /> <br /> Ash jumps up leans forward on the desk as well, and slams his hands down on the wood. The chair he was using vanishes the second he rises. &quot;You could be a dream about my own fears of empowerment,\u201d he says. \u201cYou could be a bad trip. You could be a delusion, or maybe I snorted wrong and a fly went up into my brain and vomited acid all over the parts that help me think! Maybe you're fucking Vishnu, taking on a cosmic avatar to convince me I need to murder all my pals. The sun, the moon, and the stars!&quot;<br /> <br /> Ash pulls at that connection he feels from afar, and it courses through him, winding up his arm. He wills it, and feels it crawl from his arm to his shoulders, and from his shoulders to his neck. He doesn\u2019t know what it is, but he understands power in the instinctive way only an Obrimos can. He\u2019s grinning again, his hands shaking and clenching at the 'wood' so hard they're carving furrows. He lets out a breath, and instantly his clothes are engulfed in flame, burning away from his body.<br /> <br /> &quot;But I think I know what you are, and there's something in my head right now you don't know, despite all the crap you can pull out of it, there is one thing you didn't manage, and it's something I think you'd really like to know,&quot; Ash taunts the monster across from him.<br /> <br /> Utterly unflapped by this whole display, the half-thing at the desk taps a finger a few times. Slowly, the doctor creature drawls &quot;And that is...?&quot;<br /> <br /> Ash grins slyly. &quot;Humans are better,&quot; he whispers., and rears his head back<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d the outsider manages, along with a half-second of surprise, before Ash slams his forehead into the facsimile\u2019s skull ridge.<br /> <br /> A thunderclap resounds at the impact, and the air crackles noisily as blue and golden bolts dance between Ash's open joints, his fingers, even the strands of his hair, and surge directly into the thing in front of him. It moves at his whim, dancing across and through the desk, down the creature's legs and into the floor, across the walls. And Ash, frozen in that one moment, eyes shaded and face lit up in that glow, screams a final laugh.<br /> <br /> The walls shatter. The boundaries crash. Ash sees the alien monstrosities out in space. He feels the pathway beneath him, the one Marx had tried to forge, spin and twist. He can see the vast, endlessly-shifting forms and he sees them flee before his might. He calls down the fire of the Supernal and holds it within until he blazes brighter than a star, and then he carves the pathway clear. The light becomes blinding.<br /> <br /> When the sensation lifts, Ash feels his feet on the cold metal of the observatory walkway. He can hear his own breath and heartbeat louder than ever, starting to replace the ringing in his ears. He definitely has tinnitus now if he didn't already have it before. He can hear Pathos groaning as she breaks free from whatever nightmare had been forged for her. He can hear Marx grunt as she tries to pull herself up off the metal floor.<br /> <br /> He hears something else. A quiet and gentle clinking sound, like crystal on crystal.<br /> <br /> Ash falls over, sweat on his brow. Goodness knows how long that effect had lasted. When he looks up, when he pulls himself to his feet again, leaning on an instrument console, he realizes the source of the noise: water freezing instantly at the edge of the lines Marx had carved into the wall. Crystals clinking to crystals. He doesn\u2019t believe his eyes at first. He has to move forward and put his hand near it, has to feel the sudden shift in sensation between atmosphere and none created at the lip of that doorway.<br /> <br /> Before him, like a floating blue marble, there it is, the color of an azure sky.<br /> <br /> Uranus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 05-28-2017, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T18:21:11-07:00","id":1100669,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Chapter 4: Reaching Too Far</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Part 3</b></span></span><br /> <br /> Ash gapes, transfixed by the no-longer-as-distant planet, his breath catching in his throat. The phantom pain in his forehead, the ringing in his ears, the dull ache of withdrawal\u2014they all fade to the background, diminished to near-nothing when confronted with his goal at hand. He takes a half-step forward but stops himself, suddenly remembering that this whole thing isn't just about him. The stinging in his ears rises to a faint scream as he turns around, dashing to Marx and Pathos to try and get them on their feet.<br /> <br /> &quot;I headbutted a gulmoth!&quot; are the first words out of Ash\u2019s mouth. &quot;I told it to fuck off and then I hit it in the face!&quot; he screams, as if that somehow makes it more sensible. &quot;Marx, Pathos, up! Are you alright?! Are you still sane?! Did it get to you?!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Mmmrph... Charlie, just put it in the brownies, okay? I need a few more minutes...&quot; Marx mumbles as she rolls over on her side, clearly not at fully sensibility, but Pathos bounds up the moment Ash comes near her. Her fists crackle with lightning as she jumps like a startled cat, ready to give him a good ol' punch square in the jaw. Her eyes are twitching, a cold sweat on her face as she loses her balance, staggering about a little. She looks like she had quite an experience, if she underwent a vision like he did.<br /> <br /> Ash holds up his hands defensively. &quot;Easy, easy! Just an illusion! I beat it off somehow. You're safe,\u201d he says. &quot;There are a dozen things I could say right now about what just happened-\u201c<br /> <br /> Ash glances back at the portal, eyes wide. It\u2019s there. It\u2019s all there. Validation. Vindication. There's a weight on his chest, his heart beating faster than any stimulant could ever make it.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe link between space and the Abyss,\u201d Ash starts. \u201cJust how our portals take us to where we want to go, but there's not any time.&quot; He points back to the portal. &quot;The path is clear. And I don't know how long it'll be open, if they'll come back. If Marx is going to conk it closed at any second. I'm going through. I need you to get Marx up and running. If she doesn't think it's safe to view me, give me some hours. More the better. And if she's not willing to risk bringing me back-&quot; He wets his lips, trying to think of something appropriate. &quot;Thanks. You showed me the way, and wherever it leads I wouldn't have felt alive otherwise.&quot;<br /> <br /> Pathos doesn't exactly drop her defensive, disorientated stance. She doesn't seem quite certain that Ash is real but the technobabble he spouts certainly seems familiar enough to cause her swaying to stabilize. Or perhaps that's just her inner ear getting back in order. Whatever the case, she looks at Ash with a slightly stunned expression and he is left to wonder if that is her mind still reeling or being touched by the genuine warmth.<br /> <br /> &quot;Y-... Yeah.&quot; Pathos murmurs quietly, lowering her arms. &quot;G-...&quot; She starts, letting her hands hang limply at her side for a moment, before she walks forward and gives Ash a slight push on the shoulder. &quot;Either way... whatever this is... see you on the other side.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;If you do, I'll be building the bridge down.&quot; Ash gives a stiff thumbs-up, then runs to the portal. He stops at the entrance, taking it in; his skin tingles, hairs standing on end from the remaining resonance and the gravity of the moment. He turns around, looking back towards the two women. &quot;When you tell 'em, be sure to tell them the Abyss fucking ran scared from Avery Bragg!&quot;<br /> <br /> Ash reaffixes his breathing mask, and gives them both a salute. Then he raises both fingers in a two-fingered salute, and pushes backwards towards that undiscovered country.<br /> <br /> Pathos stands there, watching half in disbelief, as Ash leaps out into the darkness. She holds up her own fingers in dull salute, before hobbling backwards to lean on the a railing as she watches Ash sail away, and Ash watches back as his window into the cosmos drifts further and further away from him.<br /> <br /> There are a lot of things that Ash doesn't notice that he\u2019d expected in space, mostly because he's compensated for them. For one, certain uncomfortable aspects of gravity are not an issue, as his internal gravity is maintained straight downwards. His temperature is regulated. There are still things that are instant and impossible to ignore: the feeling of weightlessness at the edge of his skin, the tingling sensation as any excess moisture boils away from his skin, his clothing floating and himself flying without any need for magic.<br /> <br /> More than anything is the noise. Since Awakening, since developing enough in his arcana, he\u2019s spent nearly every hour scanning or listening to the background sound of all the world\u2019s by twinning his mind: cell phone conversations, browsing the web, television transmissions\u2026 and now all there is is the background hum of the universe.<br /> <br /> Ash swallows both his spells, and suddenly the loudest things in the universe to him are his breath and heartbeat. They\u2019re almost deafeningly loud.<br /> <br /> Everything is so bright. In the distance, Ash can see the outlines of some of the moons. Why did Nixon have to say it... 'This is the greatest week in the history of the world since Creation.'<br /> <br /> There should be terror. This is the eternal dark between planets, a place of micrometeoroid strikes, a place without air, a place without life. Or so he'd known for certain until five minutes ago. But even with all that, there is no escaping the peace of it. No human being has ever journeyed this far from home, seen these sights with their own eyes. It takes a lot to keep his head, to keep the concentration needed for the immensity of this endeavor and his place in it.<br /> <br /> It had required calculated effort, out there, on Earth; studying how many newtons of thrust he can generate with his spells. Calculating both for if his velocity were maintained from Earth or if he were captured by Uranus's gravity. He'd been lucky enough to realize that he'd not need to account too greatly for it either way. Even if he'd come out totally still, he'd have been able to match the speeds within an hour or so and overtake not long after that.<br /> <br /> Ash takes a last glance at the portal. It\u2019s hard to tell if it\u2019s staying fixed in space or moving too. He shivers, angles himself, and gives the strongest push he can towards his goal, doing his best to ignore the butterflies in his stomach.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s pure chance the moon is so close. The idea had been to take pictures of it, but at this distance Ash could even go so far as to set down on it. It\u2019s an opportunity that just can't be ignored. A dull, cratered, rocky surface of grey stone with a white ring that marks a particularly unusual crater.... Hardly a winner of beauty pageants but, from where Ash is, it might be the most beautiful thing he\u2019s ever seen. He recognizes it. Umbriel. It\u2019s calling him home.<br /> <br /> At this point, Ash can't be amazed any more than he already is. At this point, between the urge to cry in relief and joy and the loud, empty-voiced scream demanding to be loosed there\u2019s no more left in him to devote to wonder. He can't get lost in it; there is work to be done here, and if what just happened was any indication, a picture from afar won't do any good.<br /> <br /> Reorienting himself, Ash falls towards Umbriel. The darkest of the moons. Truthfully, he can't say why he picked it--it seemed right.<br /> <br /> It isn't a fast journey. Ash has time to himself to think. In space, acceleration takes a while and, without the reassuring comfort of air resistance, so does slowing back down again; just as long, in fact. When he nears the ground, he\u2019s moving at perhaps half a meter a second. It\u2019s enough that his landing will be like jumping off a small chair. An immense, cratered landscape gets closer and closer--the urge to panic and bring himself to a quick halt has to be fought with every nerve in his body, just like the urge to power through it does--and slowly loses its immense perspectives until Ash is coming to a touchdown in a massive, dusty crater on the empty, barren surface of an alien moon. Another first.<br /> <br /> A second later, Ash bounds from the crater and alights on its edge. He gazes across the barren landscape. It\u2019s empty, marked only by its scars, illuminated by the sideways giant in the sky. He looks downward, at the dark regolith underneath his feet. More than that, he sees his shoes. All at once he realizes these are the first footsteps that any outer system body has ever known. He lifts his foot, staring down at the imprint, and feels sense of achievement and profound disgust. Marring the silent lands, but leaving behind proof of his accomplishment. There's a kinship to it, and he wonders back: did Armstrong and Aldrin feel this way those four decades ago?<br /> <br /> The first real footstep is a slow one, but he picks up speed. until he suddenly finds himself running across the landscape. There's no intent to it, nothing to gain. He's here, and all there is to do is explore, collect some samples, and take pictures until Marx chooses to call him back. So he runs.<br /> <br /> Bounding, leaping, barely restrained by the pull of gravity. Even without the gift of flight, Ash can jump and he\u2019ll take a good ten seconds or more to come down. If he really puts his legs into it, even longer. Turning his eyes up skyward, his material and supernal visions both see things he's never seen before: stars that did not twinkle but rather were crystal clear, shining all kinds of colors, but most the purest white. The trails of cosmic dust and debris created a beautiful haze that was the Milky Way, before becoming invisible in the light of a distant star.<br /> <br /> Ash's magical sight, meanwhile, sees what the astrologers of old had seen: streams of resonance, drifting faintly through the cosmos, the tracing and rapidly fading aura of Uranus and each of its moons. The planet's aura is far more enduring than those of its followers. Though Ash can see no spells or active portals or similar magic, he can see such brilliant colors, even smell them through his mask in a kind of electric synesthesia. It\u2019s enough that he can tell that he is in the presence of something grander than himself.<br /> <br /> Even empty space has a kind of color of its own, but Ash can't look very well at it. It is an invisible thing, but he occasionally sees in it shimmers and ripples of things he could only guess at the shapes of. The Gauntlet wears thin here; the veil between the worlds - all the worlds - wears thin. Yet, for now, he is alone. No ghosts or angels descend to praise or condemn, no tentacled horrors lurch forth from the blackness, no gods stoop to accuse him of intruding. Either they don't exist, don\u2019t care, or simply don\u2019t notice. As far as he can tell, he is alone.<br /> .<br /> No, Ash has to remind himself, not entirely alone. He\u2019s possibly closer to some things than he's ever been before. But none are reaching out, none are stalking. None prowl the world beyond. The Gauntlet reaches even past where man can reach--or did it?<br /> <br /> Ash's running slows, diminishing to hops, until finally he's still again. He looks down at his hands. It\u2019s easy to forget, between the thunder, the ghosts, the monsters. As far as man can see, because truthfully nothing is out of their grasp.<br /> <br /> Ash looks again upon Uranus. Here he is with the bastard Greek son of the solar system. He shakes his head and turns his attention back to the mission, raising the camera he\u2019d brought with him and taking a few snapshots of the surroundings. He gathers a few of the larger rocks into a pile, and then he waits.<br /> <br /> Alone, for the first time. Truly alone. No herds of ignorant, content masses. No stubborn mages, or old traditions. No Nazi lineages, or backstabbers, or faith-traitors. No sounds or smells of a world more concerned with itself than what it could be. Alone with himself and his thoughts. He closes his eyes to the universe for a moment, and soaks in the solitude, in the absolute freedom. For these few brief hours, he is unfettered by the chains of a world that drives him to despair as much as it inspires him.<br /> <br /> It isn't entirely a conscious decision to undress. First it\u2019s the tie, then the jacket. At some point the pants and underwear come off too, all neatly folded in a small pile with Winona on top, and for the first time in known history bare human ass touches the surface of another celestial body\u2014properly shielded with a small force barrier, of course. He sits beside his souvenirs with the backpack uncoupled. The breathing mask is in his hand so he can take the occasional breath, and he stares up to the stars, trying to match them up with the charts from earth.<br /> <br /> The discovery has been made. What's been discovered here, what was simply observed from the mere attempt, will possibly redefine the way the Awakened will look at the cosmos. It isn't his final goal, but it is the biggest and most important. He's proven\u2014in his mind\u2014that there's more to learn about what they are than can just be found in old books and radio static and faux-sciences. His eyes settle on the distant light that he knows is the sun. Over two and a half minutes away at lightspeed, and for a moment he wonders: if mages can hold fire, can create light, can be stone... can they be photons as well? A grasping hand rises to that small dot, closing symbolically around it. The sun, so damningly powerful that even this far out it illuminates with its reflected glory.<br /> <br /> Winona is lifted from the top of the clothes pile by strings of thought, and hovers in front of Argentum. He regards the small device. Smoke and mirrors, nothing but a tool to make his displays more believable. He sets down his mask and frowns. He closes his eyes and folds his legs in that uncomfortable pose that always causes him to lose feeling in one of them.<br /> <br /> Winona slowly undoes herself, her pieces decoupling and spreading apart in the air. Ash has been disassembling and reassembling firearms since he was a child, and yet now, looking at her like this, it feels so incredibly vulgar to be using someone else\u2019s designs, someone else\u2019s styles to work his magic. She heats up, the metals across her turning red, and the device deforms and warps. The rest of the pieces follow, twisting and warping themselves into new shapes, bending ever-so-slightly. Sleeker, bulkier, better to serve the needs of the final device.<br /> <br /> Ash works in silence, his breath still. Finally, the pieces snap back together. New pieces find their way to new homes on the modified frame. She settles softly into the soil, and Argentum opens his eyes.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s not complete; he\u2019s short some needed materials to complete the final model, but they\u2019re simple fixes. He manages a small smile as he picks the tiny thing up and holds her in his hands. One discovery would lead to others. One design would lead to more of the type. As it should be.<br /> <br /> And Ash realizes, something is different.<br /> <br /> It has all been coming to this moment, somehow. Ash would have been damn well hard-pressed to have ever said it was going to but it feels like it has. There is the thought, however intelligent or silly it might seem, that some Asimov-style psychohistorian with sufficient mastery of the right Arcana might've pieced it together; enough outsider calculation to predict the world before it happened. Maybe it\u2019s just a memory adding up from when he saw the mathematics in everything and realized how it could all, in fact, fit together. Not in the ways he ever expected, but it could.<br /> <br /> With distant light shining across Winona\u2019s new barrel, cut into a dozen different rainbow streams in Ash\u2019s mage sight, he can feel the edge of understanding - of enlightenment - just at the reaches of his perception.<br /> <br /> It has all led here. He can see the shadows of his equations in the sand before him as new numbers drift into being outwards from the Winona Mk. II. His dreams, his battles, his struggles.... He has seen spiders pour of his eyes, he has felt the horror of his family life suddenly clicking and making sense, has found friends... of a sort. People who can stand him, at least, and vice versa. His dreams of standing against the storm suddenly feel like they make sense. He can feel an... alignment. An alignment of the planets and the stars. A sensation that his next act will be portentous; a foundation stone for something bigger than he has ever imagined possible. The universe seems to hold its breath.<br /> <br /> Argentum takes a deep drag off his breather, and telekinetically lifts the rocks from his pile. No more borrowing. It can't be that anymore. His symbols need to be his own. Furrows carve themselves across the regolith of Umbriel, rocks setting themselves in places along it. Slowly, Ash marks the surface with a small message.<br /> <br /> There's too much that people can do, too much they have done to lie to the world like that, to treat the unaware like gawkers at some vulgar show. There's worlds for them to explore, to control, and to master. There's a future to build, and they deserve to see what they might build in it. With a bit of guidance, of course.<br /> <br /> 'Alone my ass,' Argentum mouths to no one, turning back to what rocks he hadn\u2019t used. The small message sits in Umbriel\u2019s dark surface. One day, absent magical interference, their probes and their telescopes will see it. And if the war isn't won by then, whatever wide-eyed and sharp-minded people will find it will see:<br /> <br /> <i>You are never alone. You can join us in the sun.</i><br /> <br /> And Ash realizes, he is different. He\u2019s shaped more than a gun, carved more than a message; these things have left their own indelible marks on him, and this one moment has shaped him. The vessel of his soul is different, and in it germinates a new legacy.<br /> <br /> Ash is left in silent contemplation in the remaining moments on Umbriel. He doesn't know how long it will last, or whether this will be the place he spends what\u2019s left of his life. Marx, when she comes around, might not be willing to risk another doozy of a Paradox like that. This could be how Ash ends his life. Worse ways to go, truthfully, and he\u2019d like to think he\u2019d be sure to cause an Awakening in a few decades time if/when a probe comes by and sees his naked corpse clutching a gun on the surface of a moon.<br /> <br /> Come what may, his return or his death, nothing can take this away from him.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, there is a faint shimmer before him and he sees those iron claws peeking through the gap in space. He sees ice form on their edges. Marx's face silently strains through the crack until Ash sees her force wide the gates once again. Waiting on the other side is not the welcome committee he had expected. Instead, there is Tartarus and four others, black keffiyehs obscuring their faces. They each are holding weapons, swords and long knives and guns with silencers. All are looking in his direction, weapons pointed towards him. Tartarus himself is at their head, two long cleavers clasped in his hands, and in a battle-ready stance.<br /> <br /> Argentum stares at the sight presented to him, his face blank of any sort of reaction. He doesn't rush for the portal, doesn't beeline in. He takes a final breath from his breathing tank, and reassembles the rods and supports in it into a crude frame, on which he hangs the breathing mask, his shades, and his clothes like some sort of MiB scarecrow. Next, he slides the camera and the rocks through the portal Marx has opened.<br /> <br /> One last time, Ash looks up towards the sun. That proves a small smile in him; it\u2019s billions of miles away, and yet right here in front of him. As a final gesture, he snags some of the background noise of the universe and twists it; a timed message, garbled just enough that it could be noise, but too distinct to just be dismissed: We are with you, and we are proud of you.<br /> <br /> With everything done, Ash hefts the last two remaining rocks. The two biggest, saved just for this moment. He hoists one over his shoulder, tucks the other near his hip, and steps through the portal.<br /> <br /> Exposed before his peers, much like last time, Ash shouts.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Look at the size of my stones! Am I not the sexiest man alive?!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<br /> <br /> The original game had Ash design a plasma pistol powered by tass on the moon. We walked that right back pretty quick once we realized what the tone of the game was becoming, and how that was pretty silly and didn't fit it at all.<br /> <br /> He forged a custom Legacy at this point in the game, and I'll be posting that once I find the write-up we did converting it from 1E to 2E. If it feels like this might be a bit early, they were growing in skill abnormally fast, and I also may have forgotten a few small adventures that happened before this; most of the players remember the broadest and most important beats, but it's likely a couple have become lost.<br /> <br /> This moment, more than anything, shapes what Ash becomes. That is not meant as a positive.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: so many tense errors. Adapting this from logs in a different tense, and I keep missing them here and there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 06-06-2017, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T07:56:08-07:00","id":1101220,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Chapter 4: Reaching Too Far</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Part 4</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> The five guardians have backed away as Ash exited the portal, now forming a ring around him. They\u2019re unmoved by his declaration.<br /> <br /> \u201cHa!\u201d Marx cheers from the back. Ash fires her a grin. Annoyed, Tartarus moves in closer, blocking their line of sight.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why, when I heard the phrases 'Paradox', 'abyssal manifestation', and 'experiment gone wrong' was the immediate thought in my head 'Ash'?&quot; Tartarus asks humorlessly, looking Ash over carefully. &quot;Set down the gear, boy. Nice and slowly. We can make this very easy for everyone.&quot; He cautions. His hands tighten on his cleavers.<br /> <br /> Ash stares at Tartarus. There are ways to read that statement, and when he takes a second to think about it\u2026 Ash realizes he doesn\u2019t care. Even Tartarus and the potential threat of death can\u2019t dampen his mood. Obediently, he drops the moon rocks to the floor.<br /> <br /> With a condescending grin, Ash focuses his attention on the chief Guardian. &quot;Gone wrong?&quot; he says in that low tone which always precedes a loud rant. &quot;Let me tell you right now, Tartarus, what you should think of when you hear Argentum Everto. You should think of the man who dared to do something none of you had the mind or the stones for. Who called down divine fire and hit a Gulmoth so hard in the face it ran away with its tail between its legs.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tartarus rolls his eyes. Of course he should\u2019ve expected this. He doesn\u2019t move to shut the Obrimos up, seemingly content to let Ash waste his breath as long as he wasn\u2019t forming an imago.<br /> <br /> \u201cWho saved-lordy yes,&quot; Ash cries, in the manner of a faith healer, &quot;-who saved one of our own Masters from the jaws of damnation itself! Hallelujah! Stared out across the void between worlds and saw the Abyss, arrayed before him, and watched as they fled in terror!&quot; His brow knits together, and his grin slowly grows wider. &quot;I flew through the empty vacuum and I made landfall over two billion miles from where we're standing now! I walked across an alien landscape, left my assprints in the sand, and saw things that could change the way we view the membrane between all worlds!\u201d<br /> <br /> One of the guardians looks pleadingly at Tartarus as Ash is busy looking up at the ceiling in triumph. Tartarus just shakes his head and mimes jerking someone off.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd more than all that, Councilor, you should damn well think of this moment!&quot; Ash pounds his chest so hard it leaves a red mark on his skin. &quot;When I, first of our kind to set foot on the outer bodies, stepped through that portal, carrying in my hands the tools for you all to do the same! And that this is the moment I announce the beginning of my grand endeavor!&quot; he finishes, his loud voice\u2014for once raised in triumph instead of anger\u2014giving way to breathless panting.<br /> <br /> The other guardians shift and move, always at the ready, and Ash gets the distinct impression that they are all looking for the first hint of aggression; the first excuse to sink a blade in him... all except Tartarus, who is looking at him with a quirked brow. For a moment, Ash sees genuine curiousity in the man's heavily scarred face before seriousness erases that pleasant intrigue.<br /> <br /> Tartarus returns rather firmly to the moment. &quot;Announce what ever you like, Ash. It is up to me whether any of it will be leaving this room.&quot; The elder declares coldly. &quot;Lay yourself face down on the floor and set your hands behind your head.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ash keeps his ridiculous grin, and slowly drops to his knees, assuming the position. &quot;Is it, councilor? I left a scarecrow on the moon. Would you use my souvenirs to retrieve it? Would you be able to ignore what it meant if you did?&quot; Ash presses his cheek to the floor.<br /> <br /> Tartarus certainly doesn't look happy with that, or how Ash had made him a party to it as a witness. But in the moment, it\u2019s not the priority. No, he waits until Ash is on the floor and then, cautiously, steps over to the young man. Ash feels a foot rest against his back and a heavy blade against the base of his neck. He\u2019s on the executioner's block.<br /> <br /> Tartarus sets one of his blades into his belt, then came the chanting in High Speech.<br /> <br /> Ash can't see the rote mudras involved. He\u2019s busy being pressed to the floor. He knows the words, though. All the Guardians chant them, adding their own potency to that of their master. The Mind and Spirit Arcana, forcibly conjoined, used together in a way that Ash cannot fathom with his limited mastery of one and complete lack of the other. He feels it, though. A blunt violation of the sanctity of his mind and soul are his reward for compliance, his memory explored and spirit searched. Not a painful experience, but an intensely unpleasant one that culminates in, at last, Tartarus lifting the blade from Ash's neck.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a moment of suspense as the younger Obrimos is left to wonder if he will next feel it drawn down on his spine.<br /> <br /> &quot;He's clean. Clean enough, anyway,&quot; Tartarus says as he steps up and off Ash\u2019s back. To Ash\u2019s surprise, he then feels a hand pull him up and guide him back to his feet. &quot;Argentum Everto, once again you prove yourself willing to take risks and put others in danger; to boldly walk where angels fear to tread.&quot; That harsh, aged voice states in a characteristic growl, yet there is a distinct lack of malice. This time, at least. Tartarus sheathes his other blade, then offers a hand to the young man to shake.<br /> <br /> Ash freezes when he sees it: Tartarus is smiling. He recovers his bearings quickly enough at the accusation\u2014that he knows how to handle.<br /> <br /> &quot;I didn't put anyone in danger,&quot; Ash protests. &quot;I asked them for help in doing something and they gave it.\u201d He takes Tartarus\u2019s hand and shakes. It\u2019s firm, steady, and aggressively vice-like at the end.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut while we're all here, if you'll consent, councilor,&quot; Ash attempts to regain some degree of formality, &quot;I\u2019d like to attempt to open a portal to where I just was using the rocks I brought back. While we have a team assembled for the worst. The barriers\u2026 they\u2019re thinner out there. I'm thinking that it was our attempt to open a portal into empty space that made it possible for the Abyss to do what it did, since what we do know suggests that it otherwise shouldn't have happened.&quot;<br /> <br /> Tartarus\u2019s brief appearance of levity takes a serious and dour downturn. He frowns sharply, but nods in permission. took his lip as he gave a nodding permission. &quot;Well, we'll find out, won't we?&quot; he says, clearly loathing the idea.<br /> <br /> The guardians move back into place around the portal. Marx looks to Ash, then to the rocks, not exactly looking eager herself. Still, she takes up the rock and does as she has agreed to do in the nervous excitement of the moment.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hm... Weird...&quot; Marx remarks as she holds the abrasive rock in her hand. &quot;Feels... Easy. Like... Way easy. Easier than even opening a portal here on Earth.&quot; She tosses the stone up and down a few times. With practiced ease, she cuts another portal in the wall and, tentatively, tears it open. She\u2019s bracing herself, bracing for a Paradox, but none come. &quot;O... kay, that's weird... I didn't... I mean, I should've...&quot; She ponders, scratching her head, then looking down at the strange rock in her palm. &quot;I didn't even have to ease the casting...&quot;<br /> <br /> Ash can't suppress the way his fists and arms shake in joy. &quot;Would you do me one more favor, Marx? I'll cast some protections and take a step out with you--we don't know if enchantments can last billions of miles from its source and I won't be testing that with people--step back through, then see if you can do it without the rock.&quot; He glances over to Tartarus. &quot;While we have a force on hand to ensure its safe.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah!&quot; Marx shouts eagerly at the opportunity to jump out onto another world.<br /> <br /> &quot;No!&quot; Tartarus answers swiftly. &quot;If she can't maintain the portal and it closes - if she can't open one from the other side - then we don't have anyone here as capable to open another. I won't risk her life on that,&quot; the elder Obrimos says with the tone of a decree.<br /> <br /> &quot;I didn't say close it when she was on the other side,&quot; Ash pouts. &quot;I'm not an imbecile.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But... space...&quot; Marx murmurs dejectedly, like a child who just got told they were too short to go on a roller coaster their friend had just gotten down from.<br /> <br /> &quot;We will need another master of Space if this is something you re eager to test in full.&quot; Tartarus continues, while his gaze sets out towards the portal. He glances briefly to Ash, then towards the moon's surface. Walking forward slowly, Tartarus draws a bag from his belt and, ever so carefully, spoons up a handful of the silt in his hand and pours it into the bag. He sets it in his belt, and then walks back to join him. &quot;A souvenir.&quot; He adds quietly under his own breath.<br /> <br /> Ash rubs his hands together before pointing at the piles of rocks and the camera. &quot;We should probably put those in a vault.&quot; He bends over and picks up one of the rocks he'd carried in. &quot;Except this. It is mine. I have named it Scraps.&quot; He glances over to Tartarus. &quot;You wouldn't happen to know another master, would you?&quot; He asks, flinging an arm around the gruff man's shoulders in a far too-friendly gesture. &quot;By the way, I have a thought experiment I want to run by you...&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=D_NHF9FrRSs\" target=\"_blank\">Tartarus quirks a brow at the thought, even as growls in disapproval. Ash is flirting with disaster, and loving it.<br /> <br /> Before Ash can continue, he hears the regular clickity-clack of plastic on metal. Heads turned. Pathos stares in shock, looking at Ash, the portal, the Guardians... Her mouth hangs briefly open. Then closed. Then open. Then closed. Her brain clicks into first gear and she frowns. The only words she can think of come immediately to mind: &quot;I thought you were going with the suit?&quot;<br /> <br /> Ash pulls away from Tartarus and looks down at himself. He looks at Pathos. He shrugs. \u201cYeah, well\u2026 let\u2019s go get fucked up!\u201d He cheers, and is met by a hoot from Marx.<br /> <br /> \u201cPants first,\u201d Tartarus reminds, dryly.<br /> <br /> As Ash, Marx, and Pathos tear down the steps of the consilium\u2019s primary meeting place\u2014Ash in an oversized pair of sweatpants and a Bad Girl t-shirt Marx has lent him\u2014Ash feels happy. A genuine giddiness is bubbling up from inside that isn\u2019t brought on by any combination of drinks or drugs. He's done it, finally, something that really, really matters, like he\u2019s always wanted, that he held on to throughout his life, that motivated him through his mystery play.<br /> <br /> That feeling stays with him through the night and into the early hours of the morning. It stays with him when Pathos leaves to get some sleep, and when Marx\u2019s circle of friends and connections show it. It stays with him through the substances they experiment with, and through the back-slaps and endless congratulations.<br /> <br /> Later that night, Ash locks himself in a bar bathroom and cries into the sink.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> m\u0310\u0306\u036b\u0305\u034b\u0367\u036f\u031b\u035c\u031e\u032f\u032e\u0317\u032b\u0326\u0359e\u030a\u034c\u0302\u030b\u0363\u033e\u0367\u030a\u0315\u0337\u032fr\u033e\u0342\u0306\u030e\u033e\u033d\u0335\u035c\u0341\u0320\u031c\u033ci\u033e\u0357\u030c\u036a\u0327\u0360\u0323 \u032b\u0329\u0319\u032c\u031c\u032a\u0326t\u0357\u0309\u0342\u0308\u0366\u0315\u0339\u0316\u033b\u0356\u0324 \u0302\u0346\u0340\u0361\u0330\u0355\u032a\u0324\u0325\u0359\u032d\u0323g\u0352\u036c\u034e\u0354\u0326\u0316\u0324\u0329a\u036d\u0351\u031a\u0365\u0350\u035e\u035f\u0330\u032d\u0359\u032b\u032c\u0317i\u0305\u0367\u030f\u0364\u036d\u0306\u0356\u032e\u0333\u0354\u032f\u0331\u031c\u032e n\u0314\u0310\u0357\u0369\u0311\u036c\u035b\u0367\u0336\u035f\u032f\u032d\u0332\u0355e\u0304\u0313\u036c\u0489\u0331\u0324\u0320\u0330\u0354\u0355\u034ed\u0368\u0365\u0300\u0351\u0304\u036c\u0328\u0335\u031f\u0355:\u0369\u036a\u0309\u036d\u0365\u0328\u032d\u0318\u0329 \u030a\u0337\u0347\u032e\u0324\u032aG\u0300\u0489\u032a\u0319\u031e\u0318\u0345r\u0367\u0302\u0369\u030f\u0343\u0366\u030a\u0352\u030d\u0335\u031b\u0354\u031d\u035a\u032ai\u036c\u0314\u0304\u0305\u030d\u0306\u034a\u0341\u0359\u0317\u0353m\u0342\u036a\u0338\u031b\u033b\u0330\u032b \u031c\u0320\u0323\u032fo\u0302\u034c\u0363\u036c\u0311\u0342\u036f\u0312\u0361\u0360\u034e\u0349\u0330\u0317\u034di\u034c\u0363\u0300\u0342\u0303\u0302\u0363\u035f\u031b\u032d\u033c\u0331\u0354\u0348r\u036d\u0346\u0308\u034c\u0314\u0338\u0332\u032e\u0324\u032d\u0356\u031e\u0355\u033b e\u036a\u036a\u031a\u0306\u0366\u0358\u0322\u0335\u0356\u031c\u0332\u0353\u031f\u0359\u0316\u035a \u036e\u0300\u0313\u036e\u0334\u0324\u0353\u035a\u0329\u034d*\u034a\u0343\u036d\u033e\u0328\u0339\u0353\u0354\u0356\u0359\u031d\u0319*\u0365\u0366\u0366\u0315\u0489\u0353\u0325<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T19:51:06-07:00","id":1102685,"title":"","content":"So since I promised myself I'd do this, here's Ash's Legacy. It grew out of watching Pathos attempt to use stage magic to inspire real magic, Ash's experiments on paradox and quiescence vis-a-vis Sleeper perception, and Ash's own jump to the edges of the solar system using legwork done by mundane Sleeper technology. It deals with the Truth, the Quiescence, and the spin a Mage can put on them by skirting the edges of and exploiting the Lie. If it looks like it might be considered a Left-Handed Path based on orthodoxy and that Ash may have learned the wrong lessons, that's a valid read.<br /> <br /> Its major sources of inspiration are secret agent fiction and the myth of the men in black.<br /> <br /> <b>For mood: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qwmk14Jj-sI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qwmk14Jj-sI<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/57LdBD0.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Legacy: Technocrat</span></b><br /> <br /> <i>Complex Machines:</i> Some yantras and attainments play off the use of complex machines, which are here defined as devices composed of 3+ moving parts or that are powered by a battery.<br /> <br /> <i>Ruling Arcanum:</i> Prime<br /> <br /> <i>Yantras:</i> Use a complex machine in casting (+1, or +2 if a battery-powered device is destroyed or depleted as a sacrament); technobabble to at least 1 Sleeper, e.g. \u201csome swamp gas reflected off Venus\u201d (+2), expose a lie or conceal the truth (+1, or +3 if this would be a sin against Wisdom), use stimulants to stay focused (+1, or +2 if this creates an adverse Condition).<br /> <br /> <i>Oblations: </i>Repair, carefully disassemble, or maintain a complex machine; craft a significant deception or unveil a significant truth; pretend to be someone else in a social setting for an hour (Shadow Names do not count); resolve a Tilt or Condition suffered by a Sleeper from Quiescence; gaslight someone<br /> <br /> <b>First: I Know You</b><br /> <i>Initiation</i><br /> The Technocrat must first understand the world he lives in, and this is best accomplished through repeated and deductive inquiry. This attainment duplicates the effects of Supernal Vision.<br /> <i>Optional: Mind *</i><br /> The Technocrat\u2019s understanding of the world and its Truth extends just as easily to the minds of the things in it. The attainment is now also capable of answering questions as Mind Scan, though seeing what it is a rock is thinking will likely return no meaningful result.<br /> <br /> <b>Second: You Don\u2019t Know Me</b><br /> <i>Prime **</i><br /> The Technocrat, understanding the nature of Truth, can hide it just as easily. This persistently cloaks the Nimbus of the Technocrat, similar to the spell Cloak Nimbus. It doesn\u2019t prevent their Immediate Nimbus from being noticed with Mage Sight, but displays it as an impersonal haze.<br /> <i>Optional: Mind **</i><br /> With an understanding of the human psyche, this ability extends to mundane perceptions. This attainment will also persistently duplicate the effects of the spell Incognito Presence, save that instead of being forgotten after the fact the Mage\u2019s features are imperfectly remembered, becoming hazy and inaccurate.<br /> <br /> <b>Third: Some Swamp Gas Reflected Off Venus</b><br /> <i>Prime ***</i><br /> Understanding the importance of discretion, the Technocrat knows how to frame the Truth in ways more palatable\u2014or obfuscate it with smoke and mirrors. The Technocrat may reflexively designate Sleepers in their immediate vicinity as Sleepwalkers for the purposes of spells cast using technocratic yantras or the Technocrat\u2019s dedicated tool if it would provide a dice bonus. This effect lasts for a scene, after which these Sleepers will be affected by the Quiescence Curse. The primary spell factor is potency.<br /> <i>Optional: Mind ***</i><br /> Provided that the Mage used a technocratic yantra or a dedicated tool that qualifies as a complex machine, at the end of a scene when a Sleeper is forced to confront the unreality of their experience they do not suffer Tilts or Conditions as a result of breaking points. This does not protect against the loss of Integrity.<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth: Ready for Anything</b><br /> <i>Prime ****</i><br /> A skilled Technocrat is dependent on his tools. An even more skilled one makes his own. The Technocrat spends 1 mana, and instantly produces a complex object no larger than Size 2 constructed as through Platonic Form. This object is suitable for use as a +1 Technocratic Yantra, and the creation of the object can count as the Yantra itself. The object vanishes after the Technocrat\u2019s following turn. If the object\u2019s use would take longer than this, such as hacking with a created laptop, it lasts only as long as it takes to finish the action. The primary spell factor is potency, and duration cannot be modified.<br /> <i>Optional: Mind ****</i><br /> Upon creating the object, the Technocrat automatically obtains ranks in the skill associated with the use of the object he created, up to the Technocrat\u2019s natural maximum. This skill vanishes when the object does. The primary spell factor is potency.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth: No Truth But My Truth</b><br /> <i>Prime *****<br /> Optional: Mind *****</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I admit, I didn't put much thought into skill requirements, since presumably Ash would meet them. At some point I'll probably do those up properly along with a write-up on what the Legacy might be like if there was more than one person running around with it for the Legacies thread.<br /> <br /> This was originally done up for 1E, but it was a garbage mess. With the advent of 2E and yantras, I had the system I needed to make it work how I wanted to. Unfortunately, I can't come up with a fifth attainment I'm satisfied with. Anyone reading this with ideas, I'd be glad to hear them. It's frustrating me.<br /> <br /> Edit: correct a few errors and clarified that a Technocrat's dedicated tool must confer a dice bonus for the spell in question to count for the third attainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":13241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","user":"Biston","date":". 06-12-2017, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}